I was doing scientific work.

500
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:28,500
- Huh?

501
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:31,467
- You're hurting me, let go.

502
00:19:31,467 --> 00:19:34,267
I heard about the Wolf
Raiders on my radio.

503
00:19:34,267 --> 00:19:35,467
That's why I reacted.

504
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:38,000
- I think he's telling
us the truth, sir.

505
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,233
- [Joel] I also
believe in fairies.

506
00:19:39,233 --> 00:19:41,167
- I don't wanna get killed.

507
00:19:41,167 --> 00:19:43,567
- Captain, UFOs on
our radar screen!

508
00:19:43,567 --> 00:19:45,667
- [Crow] I'm busy can't you see?

509
00:19:45,667 --> 00:19:46,700
- Check it.

510
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:48,033
- Yes sir.

511
00:19:48,033 --> 00:19:49,567
Let's go.
- Right.

512
00:19:49,567 --> 00:19:50,733
- [Tom] Right!

513
00:19:54,867 --> 00:19:55,733
Nice cuff links.

514
00:19:55,733 --> 00:19:56,733
- [Joel] Pierre Cardin.

515
00:19:58,867 --> 00:20:01,000
Now we're gonna
spank you big time.

516
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:03,800
- I don't want you to
move from this spot.

517
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:06,067
Unless of course you feel
like leaving this ship

518
00:20:06,067 --> 00:20:07,267
and floating in space.

519
00:20:10,033 --> 00:20:11,167
- [Crow] You can get up now.

520
00:20:12,333 --> 00:20:15,400
- [Joel] Well, it seem
comfortable but jeepers.

521
00:20:16,467 --> 00:20:17,300
- [Crow] Huh?

522
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:20,167
(whirring)

523
00:20:20,167 --> 00:20:22,667
(beeping)

524
00:20:22,667 --> 00:20:25,167
- [Tom] Hey, look that
truck's headed to Utah.

525
00:20:25,167 --> 00:20:26,267
- You keep your
eyes on the screen.

526
00:20:26,267 --> 00:20:27,167
- [Woman] Yes sir.

527
00:20:28,367 --> 00:20:29,567
- All instruments operational?

528
00:20:29,567 --> 00:20:30,400
- Yes sir.

529
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:31,933
- [Crow] And how.

530
00:20:31,933 --> 00:20:34,467
- We're approaching
route MMS 600, sir.

531
00:20:34,467 --> 00:20:36,133
- [Joel] And my heart is racing.

532
00:20:37,233 --> 00:20:39,000
- Look how fast they're going.

533
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,433
Who can generate that
kind of velocity?

534
00:20:40,433 --> 00:20:41,267
- Wolf Raiders

535
00:20:41,267 --> 00:20:42,100
- [Tom] I can.

536
00:20:42,100 --> 00:20:43,367
- For sure.

537
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:44,900
- [Crow] (sniffs)
You smell good.

538
00:20:44,900 --> 00:20:46,133
- [Pilot] Sir I don't think
we're any match for them.

539
00:20:49,433 --> 00:20:50,233
- [Crow] Got my nose.

540
00:20:50,233 --> 00:20:51,300
- Look at that!

541
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:52,133
(Crow mumbling)

542
00:20:52,133 --> 00:20:53,667
- Change course!

543
00:20:53,667 --> 00:20:55,767
You can't take them on in
this beat up old crate.

544
00:20:55,767 --> 00:20:57,033
Change course!

545
00:20:57,033 --> 00:20:58,267
- Someone put a
gag in his mouth.

546
00:20:58,267 --> 00:20:59,533
- [Tom Joe And Crow]
I'll do it, I'll do it!

547
00:20:59,533 --> 00:21:00,933
- [Tom] I got it!

548
00:21:03,533 --> 00:21:05,133
- He's talking sense for once.

549
00:21:05,133 --> 00:21:07,400
They have greater firing power.

550
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:10,200
This ship is much too old
to take on superior forces

551
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:11,433
like Wolf Raiders.

552
00:21:11,433 --> 00:21:12,667
- It's too late to
turn around now.

553
00:21:12,667 --> 00:21:14,500
I think they've
spotted our position.

554
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:17,467
- [Crow] They're bat men.

555
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:21,300
- [Joel] Are they
listening to ELO?

556
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:22,733
- Here they come.

557
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:29,867
- [Crow] It's a fleet
of drapery hooks.

558
00:21:29,867 --> 00:21:32,300
- [Joel] Are you a good
witch or a bad witch?

559
00:21:32,300 --> 00:21:33,167
- This is it.

560
00:21:33,167 --> 00:21:34,000
- [Tom] Let's go.

561
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,267
Hey, a got an idea.

562
00:21:35,267 --> 00:21:36,733
Let's get that box of
hats out of the back.

563
00:21:36,733 --> 00:21:38,100
- [Crow] Oh, I know where
that is, I'll get it.

564
00:21:51,567 --> 00:21:53,500
- At the parts--
- What are you two

565
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:55,233
yard monkeys doin' now?

566
00:21:55,233 --> 00:21:58,467
- Well, seein' the stupid
Wolf Raider hair helmets

567
00:21:58,467 --> 00:22:00,433
in the experiment reminded
me of all this stuff

568
00:22:00,433 --> 00:22:01,833
from the last hat party we had.

569
00:22:01,833 --> 00:22:02,733
Hey, put that one on.

570
00:22:02,733 --> 00:22:03,900
- Yeah.

571
00:22:03,900 --> 00:22:06,700
- Oh, no I don't
wanna, I'd feel silly.

572
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:09,533
- I remember that one, that
one was the grandest of all.

573
00:22:09,533 --> 00:22:11,400
- Yeah, yeah, I thought we
could take some of these

574
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:13,833
and have fun with them,
and maybe make up even more

575
00:22:13,833 --> 00:22:15,800
stupider hats, you know,
for the next party.

576
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:17,500
- Oh say, put that one on
me, I got an idea here.

577
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:18,833
- Okay.

578
00:22:18,833 --> 00:22:20,933
- Now you see this is
a helmet for astronauts

579
00:22:20,933 --> 00:22:21,933
who are losing their hair.

580
00:22:21,933 --> 00:22:23,100
(Crow laughing)

581
00:22:23,100 --> 00:22:23,900
When you see Mr.
Balding call him over.

582
00:22:23,900 --> 00:22:25,133
- That's a good idea.

583
00:22:25,133 --> 00:22:26,333
- Okay, all right,
I'm into it now.

584
00:22:26,333 --> 00:22:29,167
Look at this one, this
goes back to 1981.

585
00:22:29,167 --> 00:22:31,167
I'm a punk from space, get it?

586
00:22:31,167 --> 00:22:32,133
- Ooh.

587
00:22:32,133 --> 00:22:34,700
♪ I am an anarchist ♪

588
00:22:34,700 --> 00:22:35,967
Get it?

589
00:22:35,967 --> 00:22:36,900
- Oh, that's cool, hey,
this big one over here.

590
00:22:36,900 --> 00:22:37,800
Put this one on me, Joel.

591
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:38,633
- Okay.

592
00:22:38,633 --> 00:22:39,800
- Now I got, I got it.

593
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:41,533
This is what Patti
Labelle would look like

594
00:22:41,533 --> 00:22:42,500
on the space shuttle.

595
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:43,333
♪ Wah ♪

596
00:22:43,333 --> 00:22:44,400
(laughing)

597
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:46,900
- Yeah!
- Wow, that's cool.

598
00:22:46,900 --> 00:22:47,967
- try that other
one there, okay.

599
00:22:47,967 --> 00:22:49,433
- Oh, way down there.

600
00:22:49,433 --> 00:22:50,933
- Oh, oh, watch the hand.
- Sorry yeah.

601
00:22:50,933 --> 00:22:54,467
Oh, wow look it, it's the
Ted Koppel satellite of hair.

602
00:22:54,467 --> 00:22:56,267
- Or, you can pull
down the curl in front

603
00:22:56,267 --> 00:22:58,600
and it would look just
like Frank's hair helmet.

604
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:00,133
(Crow laughing)

605
00:23:00,133 --> 00:23:02,900
- Oh, I think those
things are wonderful.

606
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:04,733
(all laughing)

607
00:23:04,733 --> 00:23:06,000
- Push the button, Frank.

608
00:23:07,467 --> 00:23:09,600
- Doctor F you better
come have a look at this.

609
00:23:09,600 --> 00:23:11,500
Joel and the bots are
making fun of my hair.

610
00:23:11,500 --> 00:23:12,767
My hair!

611
00:23:12,767 --> 00:23:15,900
- Now Frank, let them
have their little fun.

612
00:23:15,900 --> 00:23:18,300
The experiment's not quite
over and they'll soon live

613
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:19,133
to regret it.

614
00:23:19,133 --> 00:23:20,167
(all laughing)

615
00:23:20,167 --> 00:23:21,433
- [Crow] Oh, rich.

616
00:23:21,433 --> 00:23:22,733
- Oh, wait, hey guys,
look at this one, hey.

617
00:23:22,733 --> 00:23:24,300
(grunting)

618
00:23:24,300 --> 00:23:26,900
This one looks like Doctor
Forrester if his head got sucked

619
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:28,700
into the vacuum of
space through a keyhole.

620
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:29,933
(laughing)

621
00:23:29,933 --> 00:23:31,167
- Now you cut that out.

622
00:23:31,167 --> 00:23:32,733
Remember what I said
about hat parties.

623
00:23:32,733 --> 00:23:34,700
You get your little hinders
back into that theater

624
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:35,933
and you watch the film.

625
00:23:35,933 --> 00:23:37,667
I'm not amused by your
antics in the least.

626
00:23:37,667 --> 00:23:39,867
- I thought it was
a sheer delight.

627
00:23:39,867 --> 00:23:43,267
I think that's about as
grand as a hat party can get.

628
00:23:43,267 --> 00:23:46,467
(buzzing)
(groaning)

629
00:23:46,467 --> 00:23:48,933
That was about as
painful as a cattle prod

630
00:23:48,933 --> 00:23:49,933
to the shoulder could get.

631
00:23:49,933 --> 00:23:52,100
(buzzing)

632
00:23:52,100 --> 00:23:53,900
- Send him commercial, Frank.

633
00:23:53,900 --> 00:23:55,933
- I'll send them
commercial sign.

634
00:23:55,933 --> 00:23:57,833
- [Jack] But later
on in the program,

635
00:23:57,833 --> 00:23:59,333
Linda Ellerbee will be out.

636
00:23:59,333 --> 00:24:00,967
(buzzing)
(groaning)

637
00:24:00,967 --> 00:24:03,567
(lively music)

638
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:10,900
- [Joe] I hate to say it but
Jack Perkins had that coming.

639
00:24:10,900 --> 00:24:12,467
- Oh, yeah, poor guy.

640
00:24:12,467 --> 00:24:13,900
- That party never
ended like that before.

641
00:24:13,900 --> 00:24:15,100
- You're crazy!

642
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:17,533
- [Tom] Ooh.

643
00:24:20,733 --> 00:24:21,567
Ooh.

644
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:25,800
(coughs)

645
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:26,667
- [Crow] I'm exhausted.

646
00:24:26,667 --> 00:24:28,933
(mimicking ship engine)

647
00:24:28,933 --> 00:24:29,933
- [Joel] I wish
someone would turn off

648
00:24:29,933 --> 00:24:32,133
the courageous cat music.

649
00:24:33,967 --> 00:24:35,533
- [Tom] Chili
peppers burn my gut.

650
00:24:39,233 --> 00:24:41,400
(singing)

651
00:24:46,600 --> 00:24:47,800
- [Crow] Ooh, chin rascal.

652
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:49,300
- [Tom] More like face rascal.

653
00:24:50,167 --> 00:24:51,200
- [Crow] Space speed.

654
00:24:54,400 --> 00:24:56,800
- [Joel] Edward Munch I presume?

655
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:58,233
- [Tom] (laughs) Look at that.

656
00:24:58,233 --> 00:24:59,900
- [Joel] Giving
him a face massage.

657
00:24:59,900 --> 00:25:01,367
- [Crow] Well we can't
fight 'em but we can confuse

658
00:25:01,367 --> 00:25:03,533
the heck out of 'em.

659
00:25:03,533 --> 00:25:06,300
(dramatic music)

660
00:25:09,333 --> 00:25:10,167
Fries are up.

661
00:25:11,267 --> 00:25:12,133
- [Tom] Yep.

662
00:25:12,133 --> 00:25:15,100
(beeping)

663
00:25:15,100 --> 00:25:16,933
- [Joel] Whoa, that was us.

664
00:25:16,933 --> 00:25:17,767
Jeepers.

665
00:25:23,133 --> 00:25:24,867
- [Tom] Somebody
hang up the phone.

666
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:30,000
Now watch out for that, ugh!

667
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:30,933
Well, never mind.

668
00:25:30,933 --> 00:25:32,100
- [Crow] Oops.

669
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:34,067
- Cease fire.

670
00:25:38,700 --> 00:25:42,600
Bacchus-3, you haven't
seen the last of me.

671
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:43,600
- [Crow] Jim Bacchus?

672
00:25:43,600 --> 00:25:45,933
(laughing)
(beeping)

673
00:25:45,933 --> 00:25:47,633
- [Joel] Uh, cookies
are done sir.

674
00:25:52,833 --> 00:25:56,033
(dramatic music)

675
00:25:56,033 --> 00:25:57,033
- [Tom] Cool, huh?

676
00:25:57,033 --> 00:25:58,133
- [Joel] Yeah, good music

677
00:25:58,133 --> 00:25:59,967
- Looks like we made it.

678
00:25:59,967 --> 00:26:02,400
- [Tom] Left each other
all the way into a knuckle.

679
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:04,267
- That's for knockin'
out my officer.

680
00:26:07,767 --> 00:26:09,700
Look alive, you guys,
there's work to do.

681
00:26:09,700 --> 00:26:11,400
- [Tom] I'm alive, sir.

682
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:13,667
- [Crow] I'm sorry
honey, are you okay?

683
00:26:13,667 --> 00:26:15,867
- [Joe] Rocky, are you
okay, say something.

684
00:26:15,867 --> 00:26:17,800
- [Tom] Yo Adrian,
cut me, cut me.

685
00:26:18,933 --> 00:26:20,667
- We did it, we
got away from them.

686
00:26:20,667 --> 00:26:23,767
- [Joel] I did,
yeah I did. (laughs)

687
00:26:23,767 --> 00:26:24,700
- Who is this guy?

688
00:26:26,133 --> 00:26:28,433
- All I know is he's 10
times as strong as we are.

689
00:26:28,433 --> 00:26:29,267
- [Tom] And I love him.

690
00:26:29,267 --> 00:26:30,400
- [Joe] And he got us

691
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:31,567
through the Wolf
Raiders single handedly.

692
00:26:31,567 --> 00:26:33,267
- [Tom] A snappy dresser
and a good friend.

693
00:26:35,100 --> 00:26:37,433
Hey bookmobile, summer
reading program.

694
00:26:41,167 --> 00:26:44,100
- [Crow] Third planet from the
sun will be known as Earth.

695
00:26:45,133 --> 00:26:45,967
Pretty much.

696
00:26:47,733 --> 00:26:49,467
- [Tom] Oh no, we'll
have to circle LaGuardia

697
00:26:49,467 --> 00:26:50,733
for an hour I'm bettin'.

698
00:26:50,733 --> 00:26:52,600
- [Joel] Hey, I can
see the Great Wall.

699
00:26:54,333 --> 00:26:56,000
- [Crow] It's okay.

700
00:26:58,300 --> 00:27:00,333
(sings)

701
00:27:00,333 --> 00:27:01,567
(dramatic music)

702
00:27:01,567 --> 00:27:03,433
- [Crow] They're goin'
to the Dells, cool.

703
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:09,300
- [Joel] Jimmy left his
Legos in the driveway again.

704
00:27:10,967 --> 00:27:13,933
- [Tom] That kid.

705
00:27:13,933 --> 00:27:17,500
You know, I tell you, that
ship is burping out a lot

706
00:27:17,500 --> 00:27:19,167
of chlorofluorocarbons there.

707
00:27:19,167 --> 00:27:20,600
Punchin' a hole in the ozone.

708
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:24,433
(Crow coughing)
- Attention please--

709
00:27:24,433 --> 00:27:27,167
- [Joel] The bank will be
closing in five minutes.

710
00:27:27,167 --> 00:27:29,600
- Landing station 14.
- Here is the latest report

711
00:27:29,600 --> 00:27:31,533
on the attack on
the Valna Raiders.

712
00:27:31,533 --> 00:27:34,100
Due to heavy damage,
aerospace port number six

713
00:27:34,100 --> 00:27:37,100
has been closed to all
traffic until further notice.

714
00:27:37,100 --> 00:27:38,000
- That's our port.

715
00:27:39,267 --> 00:27:40,700
- [Ken] What'll we do?

716
00:27:40,700 --> 00:27:42,233
- I just talked to headquarters.

717
00:27:42,233 --> 00:27:45,267
They said all streets leaving
the base have been destroyed.

718
00:27:46,667 --> 00:27:47,500
- Check that out.

719
00:27:47,500 --> 00:27:48,467
- [Tom] Check her out.

720
00:27:48,467 --> 00:27:49,533
- [Joel] Hey.

721
00:27:50,867 --> 00:27:52,733
- [Announcer] Attention please.

722
00:27:52,733 --> 00:27:55,300
- Take charge of the prisoner.
- Yes, sir.

723
00:27:55,300 --> 00:27:56,833
- [Announcer] Flights are
kindly requested to proceed

724
00:27:56,833 --> 00:27:59,767
immediately to Space Command
headquarters for debriefing.

725
00:27:59,767 --> 00:28:03,300
We repeat, senior officers
of all incoming flights

726
00:28:03,300 --> 00:28:05,733
proceed at once to Space
Command headquarters.

727
00:28:07,300 --> 00:28:10,400
- [Crow] Watch the steno
pool go wild for his vinyl.

728
00:28:11,467 --> 00:28:12,667
- Excuse me?
- Sir?

729
00:28:12,667 --> 00:28:13,600
- How can I contact
space port six?

730
00:28:13,600 --> 00:28:14,600
- Right up there, sir.

731
00:28:14,600 --> 00:28:16,067
- Thank you.

732
00:28:16,067 --> 00:28:18,467
- [Tom] I just wanna check
out my car loan here.

733
00:28:18,467 --> 00:28:19,800
Get out of my way.

734
00:28:19,800 --> 00:28:21,533
(beeping)

735
00:28:21,533 --> 00:28:22,367
- [Crow] Alt function.

736
00:28:22,367 --> 00:28:24,067
(ominous music)

737
00:28:24,067 --> 00:28:25,067
- [Tom] Huh?

738
00:28:27,267 --> 00:28:28,667
- [Joel] Noah's Ark?

739
00:28:28,667 --> 00:28:29,967
- [Tom] At the door.

740
00:28:29,967 --> 00:28:31,867
- [Crow] Hey and
there's Moses' Jeep.

741
00:28:34,267 --> 00:28:36,067
- [Tom] Ooh!

742
00:28:36,067 --> 00:28:37,800
- Did he tell you how
he got that wound?

743
00:28:37,800 --> 00:28:39,067
- [Crow] I gave it to him.

744
00:28:39,067 --> 00:28:41,500
- He refused to answer
any of our questions.

745
00:28:41,500 --> 00:28:43,900
He started shouting
and acting crazy.

746
00:28:43,900 --> 00:28:46,067
So I gave him a
tranquilizer to quiet him.

747
00:28:46,067 --> 00:28:47,500
- Is he likely to get violent?

748
00:28:47,500 --> 00:28:48,800
- He's highly unpredictable.

749
00:28:48,800 --> 00:28:50,567
Please maintain him
here under heavy guard.

750
00:28:50,567 --> 00:28:52,400
- Thanks for the warning.
- Good-bye.

751
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:53,233
Come on.

752
00:28:55,700 --> 00:28:58,167
- [Tom] Everybody's doing
their banking in this movie.

753
00:28:58,167 --> 00:28:59,633
- [Joel] Looks
like Ken's driving

754
00:28:59,633 --> 00:29:01,467
the Malibu Barbie beach jeep.

755
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:05,633
- [Tom] I just have to get out
some money for the weekend.

756
00:29:05,633 --> 00:29:09,333
Aww dang, they're closed, boy
I would love to be a banker.

757
00:29:11,033 --> 00:29:13,667
- [Joel] So, dinner
Thursday, great.

758
00:29:13,667 --> 00:29:15,033
Excuse me.
- Get out of my way.

759
00:29:15,033 --> 00:29:16,200
Beat it.

760
00:29:16,200 --> 00:29:17,967
Hi say, dinner
Friday, great, okay.

761
00:29:26,833 --> 00:29:29,533
- [Crow] Oh hi, dinner
Sunday, can we do it?

762
00:29:29,533 --> 00:29:30,367
Oh, you're free.

763
00:29:34,367 --> 00:29:37,767
- [Joel] Ladies and
gentlemen, this is Elvis.

764
00:29:37,767 --> 00:29:40,400
- [Crow] Thank you,
thank you very much, huh?

765
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:44,233
- [Tom] The audience has
left the arena. (laughing)

766
00:29:45,600 --> 00:29:47,500
- [Joel] What the, oh, huh?

767
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:50,867
- [Tom] Baby doll,
ballet slippers.

768
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:54,200
Huh, a geometric nucleus?

769
00:29:56,033 --> 00:29:56,867
And a chew toy.

770
00:29:58,800 --> 00:30:01,233
- [Crow] Well, I'll just
rifle the dead's stuff here.

771
00:30:05,567 --> 00:30:07,067
- [Joel] So dinner Sunday?

772
00:30:07,067 --> 00:30:09,233
(groaning)

773
00:30:09,233 --> 00:30:14,233
- What a gaff.
(sad music)

774
00:30:14,833 --> 00:30:16,000
- Maryanne?

775
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:18,867
- [Tom] Ginger, Skipper,
Lovey, Professor.

776
00:30:22,800 --> 00:30:26,333
- [Crow] Thank you,
thank you very much.

777
00:30:26,333 --> 00:30:27,267
- Barbara?

778
00:30:27,267 --> 00:30:28,800
- [Joel] Did he say Whopper?

779
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:29,867
- [Tom] Sounded like Whopper.

780
00:30:31,033 --> 00:30:34,067
- Is that a pet name?
- Oh darling!

781
00:30:34,067 --> 00:30:36,833
Darling, where's Maryanne?

782
00:30:36,833 --> 00:30:39,300
- [Crow] Dead,
dusting downstairs.

783
00:30:39,300 --> 00:30:40,300
- [Barbara] Where is she?

784
00:30:41,967 --> 00:30:44,333
- Maryanne's resting.

785
00:30:44,333 --> 00:30:45,333
- [Crow] In peace.

786
00:30:45,333 --> 00:30:46,433
- [Tom] Pieces.

787
00:30:46,433 --> 00:30:48,200
- Oh, thank goodness.

788
00:30:49,600 --> 00:30:50,967
I was so worried something
had happened to her

789
00:30:50,967 --> 00:30:52,533
in that terrible attack.

790
00:30:52,533 --> 00:30:54,000
- [Tom] Yeah, whatever.

791
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:56,200
- I couldn't find her
anywhere, then I passed out

792
00:30:56,200 --> 00:30:57,633
and woke up here.

793
00:30:57,633 --> 00:30:59,333
- [Tom] What'd you
say, what a view.

794
00:30:59,333 --> 00:31:00,633
You got a great room here.

795
00:31:00,633 --> 00:31:02,267
- [Barbara] Now we're
all together again.

796
00:31:03,233 --> 00:31:05,600
(Barbara gasping)

797
00:31:05,600 --> 00:31:08,400
(ominous music)

798
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:10,967
- [Joel] Well, that does
take the pressure off.

799
00:31:10,967 --> 00:31:12,033
- [Tom] Yeah.

800
00:31:12,033 --> 00:31:15,000
(dramatic music)

801
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:17,000
- [Crow] Hey, Ken's
got a problem.

802
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:18,367
- [Tom] Ken wasn't careful.

803
00:31:19,733 --> 00:31:21,000
Ken's going to get candy.

804
00:31:22,633 --> 00:31:23,900
- Oh no you don't!

805
00:31:23,900 --> 00:31:25,267
- [Doctor] Please
sir, you mustn't.

806
00:31:25,267 --> 00:31:27,333
- [Tom] Oh, yes I do, physician
heal thyself. (laughs)

807
00:31:27,333 --> 00:31:29,833
(tense music)

808
00:31:31,433 --> 00:31:32,900
- [Joel] I know just what to do.

809
00:31:32,900 --> 00:31:36,033
I'll sneak out of here
disguised as Chad Everett.

810
00:31:36,033 --> 00:31:37,333
- [Tom] That always works.

811
00:31:41,333 --> 00:31:42,967
- [Crow] Hey,
McGarret's up here.

812
00:31:46,800 --> 00:31:50,433
- [Tom] Ooh, Toughskins in
husky, slim and regular.

813
00:31:50,433 --> 00:31:53,867
- [Joel] Ken's out
cross-training, just do it.

814
00:31:53,867 --> 00:31:56,200
- [Announcer] Ken was
safe for the moment,

815
00:31:56,200 --> 00:31:58,000
but where could he go?

816
00:31:58,000 --> 00:31:58,967
What could he do?

817
00:32:00,133 --> 00:32:02,300
Outcast on his own planet.

818
00:32:02,300 --> 00:32:04,633
A fugitive alien on earth.

819
00:32:04,633 --> 00:32:06,900
He would have to make a
fresh start somewhere.

820
00:32:06,900 --> 00:32:08,167
- [Crow] In the robot holocaust.

821
00:32:08,167 --> 00:32:09,900
- [Announcer] Where, and
how could he get there?

822
00:32:09,900 --> 00:32:12,333
- [Crow] And what of
Bob's love for Chad?

823
00:32:14,100 --> 00:32:15,800
(engine roaring)

824
00:32:15,800 --> 00:32:18,400
- [Tom] Sorry, that
was me, excuse me.

825
00:32:18,400 --> 00:32:20,100
- [Ken] A spacecraft.

826
00:32:20,100 --> 00:32:21,033
- [Joel] Duh.

827
00:32:21,033 --> 00:32:22,700
- I'll have to hijack one.

828
00:32:22,700 --> 00:32:23,700
- [Joel] (laughs) Better.

829
00:32:23,700 --> 00:32:25,133
- [Crow] Not in those slacks.

830
00:32:27,633 --> 00:32:29,800
(singing)

831
00:32:32,267 --> 00:32:35,833
- [Joel] Now, now, I cue myself,
jump back and ha, jumping,

832
00:32:35,833 --> 00:32:37,333
running and spinning.

833
00:32:37,333 --> 00:32:38,300
- [Tom] Follow me, follow me.

834
00:32:42,100 --> 00:32:44,633
Oh, I'm over here, careful.

835
00:32:44,633 --> 00:32:46,633
(Tom panting)

836
00:32:46,633 --> 00:32:48,200
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight,

837
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:51,267
nine, 10, 11, 12,
13, 14, 15, 16, 17.

838
00:32:52,433 --> 00:32:54,200
- [Joel] This is
good for the glutes.

839
00:32:54,200 --> 00:32:55,467
- [Tom] Push, push guys.

840
00:32:55,467 --> 00:32:57,800
The burn, the burn. (panting)

841
00:33:01,667 --> 00:33:05,100
- [Joel] He's at a ski
lodge now, what gives?

842
00:33:05,100 --> 00:33:06,500
- [Tom] Excuse me,
can you tell me where

843
00:33:06,500 --> 00:33:08,667
I could hijack a
spaceship anybody?

844
00:33:08,667 --> 00:33:09,633
Okay, never mind.

845
00:33:10,900 --> 00:33:11,733
Anybody?

846
00:33:12,733 --> 00:33:13,667
Spaceship?

847
00:33:13,667 --> 00:33:14,900
I need to hijack a spaceship.

848
00:33:17,067 --> 00:33:17,900
Say!

849
00:33:19,067 --> 00:33:21,400
- [Ken] Nobody around,
but how do I get aboard?

850
00:33:22,567 --> 00:33:24,000
- [Tom] Go through
the lumber yard.

851
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:26,167
That's how you get a board,
get it, I said lumber?

852
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:28,833
- Hello, stranger.

853
00:33:28,833 --> 00:33:30,333
- [Crow] Hi, sailor.

854
00:33:30,333 --> 00:33:32,467
- Did you just drop by for
coffee or are were you planning

855
00:33:32,467 --> 00:33:33,867
to stay on for
the cocktail hour?

856
00:33:33,867 --> 00:33:34,967
- [Crow] Huh?

857
00:33:37,300 --> 00:33:38,733
I'll have that cocktail now.

858
00:33:40,767 --> 00:33:44,100
- Well friend, you're not
a very gracious guest.

859
00:33:44,100 --> 00:33:45,600
- [Crow] I've brought crackers.

860
00:33:45,600 --> 00:33:47,033
- It isn't very courteous
to point a gun at your host.

861
00:33:47,033 --> 00:33:48,700
- [Joel] It's not courteous
to point your finger--

862
00:33:48,700 --> 00:33:49,633
- You shouldn't have run away

863
00:33:49,633 --> 00:33:51,000
from that nice clean infirmary.

864
00:33:52,033 --> 00:33:53,067
How about--
- St. James infirmary.

865
00:33:53,067 --> 00:33:54,233
- [Joe] Giving me the gun?

866
00:33:54,233 --> 00:33:55,733
- That's enough.

867
00:33:55,733 --> 00:33:57,167
Turn around and face the wall.

868
00:33:57,167 --> 00:33:58,000
- [Joel] The wall?

869
00:33:58,000 --> 00:33:58,867
- Go on!

870
00:33:58,867 --> 00:34:01,267
(Joe laughing)

871
00:34:01,267 --> 00:34:02,367
- [Joe] Don't you think
it'd be a good idea

872
00:34:02,367 --> 00:34:03,300
to check if it's loaded?

873
00:34:03,300 --> 00:34:04,133
- What?

874
00:34:04,133 --> 00:34:05,400
(grunting)

875
00:34:05,400 --> 00:34:08,200
- [Joel] Room 235,
works every time.

876
00:34:08,200 --> 00:34:09,467
- [Crow] Honest, Joel.

877
00:34:09,467 --> 00:34:10,933
- Stupidest thing I ever
did was to save the life

878
00:34:10,933 --> 00:34:13,100
of a Valna Raider, You people
have no respect for life!

879
00:34:13,100 --> 00:34:14,633
You'd even kill your
own families if it

880
00:34:14,633 --> 00:34:16,433
brought you some advantage.

881
00:34:16,433 --> 00:34:18,933
The world will never be safe
with people like you around!

882
00:34:18,933 --> 00:34:20,133
- [Joel] Let's kiss.

883
00:34:20,133 --> 00:34:21,900
- Look, you'd even
destroy the universe!

884
00:34:21,900 --> 00:34:23,567
Look in.

885
00:34:23,567 --> 00:34:25,833
The minute I saw you, I
knew you were one of those

886
00:34:25,833 --> 00:34:27,700
savage Valna Wolves.

887
00:34:27,700 --> 00:34:28,900
- [Tom] But I loved you!

888
00:34:30,300 --> 00:34:32,900
(lively music)

889
00:34:36,433 --> 00:34:38,733
- You know something,
that was my last flight.

890
00:34:38,733 --> 00:34:42,133
I wanted to devote the rest
of my life to my wife and kid.

891
00:34:42,133 --> 00:34:44,533
My wife just died in my arms!

892
00:34:44,533 --> 00:34:46,233
- [Crow] Hey, you were
way over by the window.

893
00:34:46,233 --> 00:34:47,167
- [Tom] Yeah.

894
00:34:47,167 --> 00:34:49,300
- Honestly, where's the pride

895
00:34:49,300 --> 00:34:51,700
in killing defenseless
women and children?

896
00:34:51,700 --> 00:34:53,300
You call that heroism?

897
00:34:53,300 --> 00:34:55,833
- [Crow] I call it fun,
don't you have any hobbies?

898
00:34:57,167 --> 00:34:59,867
- When we saved you, a
little swatch of cloth

899
00:34:59,867 --> 00:35:01,300
got torn off your uniform.

900
00:35:01,300 --> 00:35:02,233
- [Tom] Ooh.

901
00:35:02,233 --> 00:35:04,433
- I found one exactly like it

902
00:35:04,433 --> 00:35:06,600
next to the body of
my little daughter!

903
00:35:06,600 --> 00:35:08,967
What have you got to say?

904
00:35:08,967 --> 00:35:10,500
- [Tom] Oops, I'm sorry?

905
00:35:10,500 --> 00:35:11,633
- I'm listening!
- Ah!

906
00:35:13,533 --> 00:35:15,800
(shouting)

907
00:35:17,133 --> 00:35:18,733
- [Crow] No one can
beat me at snap zooms.

908
00:35:18,733 --> 00:35:20,367
I was in Time of the Apes.

909
00:35:20,367 --> 00:35:22,467
- There's no point
trying to hide it.

910
00:35:22,467 --> 00:35:24,067
I was on a mission.

911
00:35:24,067 --> 00:35:26,433
But I killed one of my
comrades in an accident.

912
00:35:27,367 --> 00:35:28,667
I ran away.

913
00:35:28,667 --> 00:35:29,900
- [Tom] Nice lips.

914
00:35:29,900 --> 00:35:31,833
- Now the other Wolves
are hunting the traitor.

915
00:35:31,833 --> 00:35:33,767
- You're lying
through your teeth.

916
00:35:33,767 --> 00:35:34,700
You expect me to buy that?

917
00:35:34,700 --> 00:35:36,367
- It's the truth, I swear it!

918
00:35:36,367 --> 00:35:37,900
Now listen to the
rest of the story!

919
00:35:37,900 --> 00:35:39,600
- [Tom] Page two.

920
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:41,267
- We attacked Earth.

921
00:35:41,267 --> 00:35:42,900
My buddy ordered
me to kill a child.

922
00:35:42,900 --> 00:35:44,700
- [Joel] They never
explain the blonde wigs.

923
00:35:44,700 --> 00:35:46,167
I don't get that.

924
00:35:46,167 --> 00:35:48,733
- I couldn't and it was then
that he turned his rifle

925
00:35:48,733 --> 00:35:49,567
on the child.

926
00:35:50,700 --> 00:35:53,600
Then I saw him raise
his gun to fire.

927
00:35:54,767 --> 00:35:56,567
I just wanted to get him
to put the rifle down.

928
00:35:56,567 --> 00:35:58,867
(zapping)

929
00:35:58,867 --> 00:36:02,367
Suddenly, I looked down
and saw that glassy look

930
00:36:02,367 --> 00:36:03,633
in his eyes.

931
00:36:03,633 --> 00:36:04,867
- [Tom] That sly,
come-hither stare.

932
00:36:04,867 --> 00:36:06,233
- I'd forgotten
how strong I was.

933
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:09,100
- Ken, you did the right thing.

934
00:36:09,100 --> 00:36:09,967
- [Joel] Now turn
off the chants.

935
00:36:09,967 --> 00:36:11,600
- The world is mad.

936
00:36:11,600 --> 00:36:14,300
You know I never keep
any bullets in my gun.

937
00:36:14,300 --> 00:36:15,567
- [Crow] Like Barney Fife.

938
00:36:15,567 --> 00:36:17,533
- The thought of killing
anyone is too horrible.

939
00:36:17,533 --> 00:36:20,933
I didn't feel that way
when I was about your age.

940
00:36:20,933 --> 00:36:22,867
I was like you,
wild and reckless.

941
00:36:22,867 --> 00:36:24,833
- [Joel] That's me to a T.

942
00:36:24,833 --> 00:36:26,400
- Until today you
killed for kicks.

943
00:36:26,400 --> 00:36:28,600
- [Crow] Hey, like
the "Wild Rebels".

944
00:36:28,600 --> 00:36:31,133
- You were just like I used
to be, a thrill killer.

945
00:36:31,133 --> 00:36:33,700
- I wasn't, I was a soldier
carrying out orders!

946
00:36:33,700 --> 00:36:35,200
There's no dishonor in that!

947
00:36:35,200 --> 00:36:37,200
- [Joe] What is dishonor then?

948
00:36:37,200 --> 00:36:38,800
Killing for a corrupt power?

949
00:36:38,800 --> 00:36:40,033
- [Joel] Punky cheeks.

950
00:36:40,033 --> 00:36:41,800
- [Joe] You betrayed
your own country.

951
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:44,000
(grunting)

952
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:46,233
(chanting)

953
00:36:48,067 --> 00:36:51,767
- You betrayed us, you traitor.

954
00:36:51,767 --> 00:36:54,133
- [Crow] See that's why
you're a scummy traitor.

955
00:36:55,267 --> 00:36:56,100
- Cigar.

956
00:36:56,100 --> 00:36:57,467
- [Tom] Why, yes it is.

957
00:36:57,467 --> 00:36:58,833
(Joe laughing)

958
00:36:58,833 --> 00:37:00,533
- I've been thinking
things over.

959
00:37:01,467 --> 00:37:02,900
No point in retiring now

960
00:37:04,833 --> 00:37:07,500
with no wife or
family to go home to.

961
00:37:07,500 --> 00:37:08,967
- [Joel] You'll do fine.

962
00:37:08,967 --> 00:37:11,733
- You know, I'm going to need
some new men in the crew.

963
00:37:11,733 --> 00:37:14,100
- [Crow] Slim-hipped
and willowy.

964
00:37:14,100 --> 00:37:15,333
- [Tom] Big lips.

965
00:37:15,333 --> 00:37:18,233
- Young fella who's
become a fugitive.

966
00:37:19,367 --> 00:37:21,700
Who's being hunted
all over the universe.

967
00:37:21,700 --> 00:37:22,933
- [Tom] Who could that be?

968
00:37:22,933 --> 00:37:26,033
- Could do a lot worse
than throwing in his lot

969
00:37:26,033 --> 00:37:27,933
with the crew of Bacchus-3.

970
00:37:27,933 --> 00:37:29,167
- [Tom] Hm.

971
00:37:29,167 --> 00:37:31,000
- We might even
get to be friends.

972
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:32,467
- [Crow] He asked
me, he asked me!

973
00:37:32,467 --> 00:37:34,600
- I don't understand, what
have a I done to deserve this?

974
00:37:34,600 --> 00:37:37,000
- We don't deserve
half the things we get.

975
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:39,233
(laughing)

976
00:37:43,633 --> 00:37:44,600
You're stuck here!

977
00:37:45,667 --> 00:37:46,600
Listen.

978
00:37:46,600 --> 00:37:48,100
- [Tom] Mood swings, boy.

979
00:37:48,100 --> 00:37:50,033
- Do exactly what I tell you
and you have a good chance

980
00:37:50,033 --> 00:37:52,900
of turning into a man,
not just a Wolf Raider.

981
00:37:52,900 --> 00:37:54,900
(Tom growling)

982
00:37:54,900 --> 00:37:56,200
And don't you ever forget.

983
00:37:57,433 --> 00:37:58,900
- [Tom] What?

984
00:37:58,900 --> 00:38:00,133
- I know exactly who you
are and where you came from.

985
00:38:00,133 --> 00:38:01,400
- [Tom] Oh.

986
00:38:01,400 --> 00:38:02,933
- One false move and
I'll set you adrift

987
00:38:02,933 --> 00:38:04,267
to fend for yourself.

988
00:38:05,133 --> 00:38:06,333
- [Woman] Captain!

989
00:38:06,333 --> 00:38:07,500
- [Joel] Now let's
have some fun.

990
00:38:07,500 --> 00:38:08,367
- Now then.

991
00:38:08,367 --> 00:38:09,300
- [Woman] Captain!

992
00:38:09,300 --> 00:38:10,100
- Whether you like it or not.

993
00:38:10,100 --> 00:38:11,300
- [Tom] She's yours.

994
00:38:11,300 --> 00:38:13,133
- It looks like
you just signed on.

995
00:38:13,133 --> 00:38:15,000
- [Crow] Welcome to Herbalife.

996
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:16,800
(dramatic music)

997
00:38:16,800 --> 00:38:17,600
- Captain Joe.

998
00:38:19,800 --> 00:38:21,333
(Ken laughing)

999
00:38:21,333 --> 00:38:23,000
I kinda think I'll like it.

1000
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:25,667
- [Crow] Yeah, whatever, idiot.

1001
00:38:26,767 --> 00:38:28,333
- [Joel] Let's go skiing gang.

1002
00:38:28,333 --> 00:38:29,167
- Everything's fine.

1003
00:38:29,167 --> 00:38:31,400
(dramatic music)

1004
00:38:31,400 --> 00:38:35,333
- [Joel] In the land of Dairy
Queen, we treat you right.

1005
00:38:35,333 --> 00:38:37,100
- [Narrator] While
Ken was being welcomed

1006
00:38:37,100 --> 00:38:40,767
aboard Bacchus-3 and starting
his life as an earthling,

1007
00:38:40,767 --> 00:38:44,333
back on Valnastar, Ken's
former home, the Wolf Raiders

1008
00:38:44,333 --> 00:38:45,867
were returning from their
unsuccessful mission.

1009
00:38:45,867 --> 00:38:48,167
- [Crow] Backstory.

1010
00:38:48,167 --> 00:38:50,500
- [Narrator] Their leader,
the notorious Lord Halkun,

1011
00:38:50,500 --> 00:38:52,033
who was determined

1012
00:38:52,033 --> 00:38:54,500
to punish Ken mercilessly
for his supposed betrayal.

1013
00:38:54,500 --> 00:38:57,400
- [Tom] Meanwhile, I went
to more voiceover auditions.

1014
00:39:04,100 --> 00:39:07,700
- [Joel] Say, speak of
punishing mercilessly, whoa.

1015
00:39:07,700 --> 00:39:09,733
(whistling)

1016
00:39:09,733 --> 00:39:12,433
- [Crow] I'm wearing a
bib 'cause I just ate.

1017
00:39:12,433 --> 00:39:14,500
- [Tom] Tragedy
tomorrow, kabuki tonight.

1018
00:39:14,500 --> 00:39:16,367
- I take it you have already
heard that your brother

1019
00:39:16,367 --> 00:39:17,733
has lost his life.

1020
00:39:17,733 --> 00:39:18,633
- Yes.

1021
00:39:18,633 --> 00:39:20,233
- He was killed by Ken.

1022
00:39:20,233 --> 00:39:21,067
- Ken did it?

1023
00:39:21,067 --> 00:39:22,000
- [Tom] Those bastards.

1024
00:39:22,000 --> 00:39:23,500
- Why, that can't be true.

1025
00:39:23,500 --> 00:39:25,500
- I know it must
seem impossible.

1026
00:39:25,500 --> 00:39:28,100
You loved each other, and he
was your brother's friend.

1027
00:39:28,100 --> 00:39:29,700
I trusted him too.

1028
00:39:29,700 --> 00:39:32,833
How sad it is to put
your trust in a traitor.

1029
00:39:32,833 --> 00:39:34,833
And that's not the worst part.

1030
00:39:34,833 --> 00:39:37,767
He killed your brother in an
attempt to defend an earthling.

1031
00:39:37,767 --> 00:39:38,967
- [Joel] Oops.

1032
00:39:38,967 --> 00:39:40,433
- [Tom] Now, we'll never
get my records back.

1033
00:39:40,433 --> 00:39:42,567
- Then he escaped into the
unknown in a stolen spaceship.

1034
00:39:42,567 --> 00:39:44,000
- [Joel] That'll happen.

1035
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:47,233
- He's a coward and a traitor,
he has disgraced us all.

1036
00:39:47,233 --> 00:39:48,500
- [Crow] I forbid
you to see him.

1037
00:39:48,500 --> 00:39:50,500
- He has forfeited
the right to live.

1038
00:39:50,500 --> 00:39:51,867
- Must he die?

1039
00:39:51,867 --> 00:39:54,433
- [Halkun] Yes and you
must be his executioner.

1040
00:39:54,433 --> 00:39:57,800
It is an old Valna law that
murders must be avenged

1041
00:39:57,800 --> 00:39:59,067
by the victim's next of kin.

1042
00:39:59,067 --> 00:40:01,233
- [Tom] Not that I don't
trust you, oh wise one,

1043
00:40:01,233 --> 00:40:03,467
but can I see the
book on that rule?

1044
00:40:06,167 --> 00:40:07,933
- [Crow] Rat Patrol, in color.

1045
00:40:13,000 --> 00:40:14,500
- [Joel] You know, it looks
like they were shooting this

1046
00:40:14,500 --> 00:40:16,833
out of the windshield of a
Vista Cruiser station wagon.

1047
00:40:16,833 --> 00:40:18,433
- [Tom] Yeah, tinted.

1048
00:40:19,800 --> 00:40:22,333
- [Halkun] Ken must
die by your hand.

1049
00:40:22,333 --> 00:40:25,600
You are not to return
here without his head.

1050
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:27,000
Without his head.

1051
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:29,300
- [Joel] Oh, I gotta
lay off the 'shrooms.

1052
00:40:30,200 --> 00:40:31,033
- Ken.

1053
00:40:31,900 --> 00:40:33,533
- [Crow] Did someone say Ken?

1054
00:40:35,900 --> 00:40:38,667
- Ken, you will pay
dearly for what you did.

1055
00:40:38,667 --> 00:40:41,133
- [Joel] I know, Mama.

1056
00:40:41,133 --> 00:40:42,333
- [Crow] Oh!

1057
00:40:42,333 --> 00:40:43,633
- [Tom] Well, that was easy.

1058
00:40:43,633 --> 00:40:45,733
I can go home, oh damn,
I was supposed to bring

1059
00:40:45,733 --> 00:40:46,967
back his head.

1060
00:40:46,967 --> 00:40:48,100
- [Woman] Ken!

1061
00:40:49,567 --> 00:40:51,633
- [Tom] Where aren't you?

1062
00:40:53,767 --> 00:40:55,867
- [Joel] Is she gonna need a
ride out there or somethin'?

1063
00:40:55,867 --> 00:40:57,200
- [Crow] I don't know.

1064
00:40:57,200 --> 00:40:59,500
- [Tom] You're supposed
to walk to the revenge.

1065
00:41:03,433 --> 00:41:05,000
- I know you've heard
of the Star Kararu.

1066
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:07,100
It's in the center of the
seventh constellation.

1067
00:41:07,100 --> 00:41:09,433
- Inhabited by a strong
and independent nation.

1068
00:41:09,433 --> 00:41:11,567
- [Joel] The Cherokee Nation.

1069
00:41:11,567 --> 00:41:13,733
- We have been aligned
with Kararu for centuries.

1070
00:41:13,733 --> 00:41:15,567
And now they are threatened.

1071
00:41:15,567 --> 00:41:18,000
Their mortal enemies have
developed a super weapon.

1072
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:19,133
- Super weapon?

1073
00:41:19,133 --> 00:41:20,533
- [Crow] Well, a
really good one anyway.

1074
00:41:20,533 --> 00:41:22,367
- I don't have all the
details but we have

1075
00:41:22,367 --> 00:41:23,933
an intelligence report.

1076
00:41:23,933 --> 00:41:26,400
Apparently this weapon can
destroy a whole continent.

1077
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:28,733
If we do nothing to prevent
it than I'm afraid Kararu

1078
00:41:28,733 --> 00:41:30,933
is doomed to extinction.

1079
00:41:30,933 --> 00:41:33,167
And that is the reason that
they got in touch with us.

1080
00:41:33,167 --> 00:41:34,367
- [Tom] Now we're alone.

1081
00:41:34,367 --> 00:41:36,200
- After giving it
careful consideration,

1082
00:41:36,200 --> 00:41:38,300
I've decided that you
are the only man capable

1083
00:41:38,300 --> 00:41:39,533
of doing the job.

1084
00:41:39,533 --> 00:41:40,933
- [Tom] So we're going
to get you a new dickey.

1085
00:41:40,933 --> 00:41:42,967
- But they've always
handled their own defenses.

1086
00:41:42,967 --> 00:41:44,800
- This time they've got
more than one enemy.

1087
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:46,333
- [Tom] Pool table.

1088
00:41:46,333 --> 00:41:48,500
- It looks like the Valna
Raiders are going to attack.

1089
00:41:48,500 --> 00:41:50,367
Valnastar is one of
the strongest forces

1090
00:41:50,367 --> 00:41:51,800
of evil in our universe.

1091
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:53,267
- [Crow] See, what'd I tell you?

1092
00:41:53,267 --> 00:41:57,267
(booming)
(dramatic music)

1093
00:41:57,267 --> 00:41:58,733
- [Joel] What gives?

1094
00:41:58,733 --> 00:42:01,167
- [Tom] Flashback, I don't know.

1095
00:42:01,167 --> 00:42:02,633
- [Crow] It's cool anyway.

1096
00:42:02,633 --> 00:42:04,400
- [Joel] Huh, I'm sorry,
I was just playin'

1097
00:42:04,400 --> 00:42:05,800
a video game in my head.

1098
00:42:07,600 --> 00:42:08,533
- I understand.

1099
00:42:09,700 --> 00:42:12,333
There's no way that they
can handle this alone.

1100
00:42:12,333 --> 00:42:15,733
- [Man Of Left] Yes, the
Kararuns are a valiant people

1101
00:42:15,733 --> 00:42:18,767
but they are no match
for the Valna Raiders.

1102
00:42:18,767 --> 00:42:20,467
- [Tom] Huh what, you
were talkin' to me?

1103
00:42:20,467 --> 00:42:21,933
Oh, I'm sorry, I was
thinking of the eighth hole

1104
00:42:21,933 --> 00:42:23,500
at Torrey Pines, sorry.

1105
00:42:25,333 --> 00:42:26,567
- [Joel] Let's cut
the crap, I love you.

1106
00:42:26,567 --> 00:42:27,567
- Very well.

1107
00:42:28,633 --> 00:42:29,667
I accept the mission.

1108
00:42:31,100 --> 00:42:34,067
- Good, excellent, I knew
you wouldn't disappoint us.

1109
00:42:34,067 --> 00:42:35,600
- [Joel] Yuck.

1110
00:42:35,600 --> 00:42:37,300
- [Man] I always look
forward to the crew check,

1111
00:42:37,300 --> 00:42:38,900
especially with such
a fine crew as the one

1112
00:42:38,900 --> 00:42:39,700
on the Bacchus-3.

1113
00:42:39,700 --> 00:42:40,700
- [Tom] I love it.

1114
00:42:40,700 --> 00:42:41,633
- [Joe] That's Rocky.

1115
00:42:41,633 --> 00:42:42,900
- [Tom] The flying squirrel.

1116
00:42:42,900 --> 00:42:44,400
- [Joe] The best space
pilot in the business.

1117
00:42:44,400 --> 00:42:45,967
- [Joel] And a good friend.

1118
00:42:45,967 --> 00:42:47,600
- [Joe] You remember
Dan, my navigator.

1119
00:42:47,600 --> 00:42:48,500
- [Ken] Indeed I do.

1120
00:42:48,500 --> 00:42:50,133
(laughs)

1121
00:42:50,133 --> 00:42:51,467
Oh, and this little darling

1122
00:42:51,467 --> 00:42:53,700
is your morale officer no doubt.

1123
00:42:53,700 --> 00:42:55,200
- [Man] Negative, sir.

1124
00:42:55,200 --> 00:42:58,133
The Lieutenant knows more
than the two us put together.

1125
00:42:58,133 --> 00:42:59,633
- [Ken] You don't say.

1126
00:42:59,633 --> 00:43:02,700
- Doesn't sound half bad.
- Young Billy,

1127
00:43:02,700 --> 00:43:04,567
he's going to make a
fine officer some day.

1128
00:43:04,567 --> 00:43:06,600
- It's a good crew, Joe.
- Not quite finished, sir.

1129
00:43:06,600 --> 00:43:08,600
- [Crow] Now I've got some
shots of the picnic here.

1130
00:43:11,767 --> 00:43:13,233
- Who's the busboy?
- A new face.

1131
00:43:13,233 --> 00:43:15,300
He looks like he could
handle himself in a fight.

1132
00:43:15,300 --> 00:43:16,967
- [Joe] Oh, he's rough
and ready all right.

1133
00:43:16,967 --> 00:43:18,867
But that's just what I
need on this mission.

1134
00:43:18,867 --> 00:43:20,100
- A real bruiser.

1135
00:43:20,100 --> 00:43:21,500
- [Joe] After all,
the Valna Raiders--

1136
00:43:21,500 --> 00:43:22,900
- [Tom] Send him to my room.

1137
00:43:24,133 --> 00:43:26,633
- Listen Joe, we're
asking you to set out

1138
00:43:26,633 --> 00:43:28,633
on a dangerous assignment.

1139
00:43:28,633 --> 00:43:31,100
We can't afford any unknown
quantities out there.

1140
00:43:31,100 --> 00:43:33,667
Do you know anything about
this man's background?

1141
00:43:33,667 --> 00:43:35,033
- I just wanna recruit this guy.

1142
00:43:35,033 --> 00:43:36,467
- [Crow] In the worst way.

1143
00:43:36,467 --> 00:43:38,300
- I wasn't planning
to adopt him.

1144
00:43:38,300 --> 00:43:40,000
- Joe, I like you.

1145
00:43:41,100 --> 00:43:42,567
- [Crow] But you're weird.

1146
00:43:42,567 --> 00:43:45,667
- Okay, if you think he's all
right than he's all yours.

1147
00:43:45,667 --> 00:43:48,633
- [Tom] Whoa, I'm in
China, I'm in China.

1148
00:43:48,633 --> 00:43:50,533
Oh no, it's just the...

1149
00:43:50,533 --> 00:43:54,133
- [Joel] Red ball jets help
you run faster, jump higher.

1150
00:43:54,133 --> 00:43:54,967
- [Tom] Cool.

1151
00:43:58,700 --> 00:44:01,600
Oh, I thought I was in
a Nestea commercial.

1152
00:44:04,000 --> 00:44:06,133
- [Crow] Oh, I see a bunny
and a cloud and a blonde wig

1153
00:44:06,133 --> 00:44:08,400
and a satin tap pant.
(gentle music)

1154
00:44:08,400 --> 00:44:09,700
- [Tom] Matching camisole.

1155
00:44:11,100 --> 00:44:12,567
- [Crow] If you do it right.

1156
00:44:12,567 --> 00:44:14,600
- [Tom] Another royalty check
for Herb Alpert coming up.

1157
00:44:14,600 --> 00:44:16,267
- [Joel] Some calf
muscles there.

1158
00:44:20,800 --> 00:44:25,333
I want your wig now!

1159
00:44:25,333 --> 00:44:27,600
- [Crow] It's been 26 miles.

1160
00:44:27,600 --> 00:44:30,400
It's only fun if I
catch you, wait up!

1161
00:44:32,500 --> 00:44:35,600
♪ It's a tangled storm of love ♪

1162
00:44:35,600 --> 00:44:38,100
- [Joel] Come on, it's my
turn to wear the night gown.

1163
00:44:38,100 --> 00:44:40,000
- [Tom] We gotta go folks.

1164
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:40,933
- [Crow] Let's run.

1165
00:44:42,533 --> 00:44:44,533
- Rita.

1166
00:44:44,533 --> 00:44:47,033
Try to understand,
I did what I had to.

1167
00:44:48,567 --> 00:44:51,167
(lively music)

1168
00:44:54,600 --> 00:44:57,533
- Okay, now Crow, I
want you to be Ken.

1169
00:44:57,533 --> 00:45:00,633
And Tom I want you to be Ken.

1170
00:45:00,633 --> 00:45:02,133
- Joel, I feel ridiculous.

1171
00:45:02,133 --> 00:45:05,233
I'm dressed like Evel
Knievel only not so tasteful.

1172
00:45:05,233 --> 00:45:07,567
- Yeah Joel, I don't
wanna cast aspersions

1173
00:45:07,567 --> 00:45:09,033
on your little play-acting idea.

1174
00:45:09,033 --> 00:45:12,100
I don't wanna be the dead
squirrel under the floorboards

1175
00:45:12,100 --> 00:45:13,533
of your huntin' shack.

1176
00:45:13,533 --> 00:45:15,000
But this is the stupidest thing
you've ever had us do yet!

1177
00:45:15,000 --> 00:45:17,067
- Yeah Joe, you been
nippin' at the tester's glue

1178
00:45:17,067 --> 00:45:18,567
or what here?

1179
00:45:18,567 --> 00:45:19,967
- Come on, I just thought
it would be fun to play

1180
00:45:19,967 --> 00:45:22,567
the handsome captain
of the spaceship, okay?

1181
00:45:22,567 --> 00:45:24,633
It's a lark, a spoon,
run with me on this one.

1182
00:45:24,633 --> 00:45:26,867
I promise I'll never
make you do it again.

1183
00:45:26,867 --> 00:45:28,300
- Yeah, right.

1184
00:45:28,300 --> 00:45:29,533
Well, give it a week
I'll have a six-foot foam

1185
00:45:29,533 --> 00:45:31,767
scorpion stinger
hanging off my butt.

1186
00:45:31,767 --> 00:45:33,033
- Come on.

1187
00:45:33,033 --> 00:45:34,233
- Look, let's just get
this over with, okay?

1188
00:45:34,233 --> 00:45:35,800
- Just come on you
guys, it'll be a gas.

1189
00:45:35,800 --> 00:45:37,700
Okay, Cambot help
me out on this one.

1190
00:45:37,700 --> 00:45:40,467
Neutral drive off,
engines to full.

1191
00:45:40,467 --> 00:45:41,367
- All right, Ken.

1192
00:45:42,700 --> 00:45:44,633
- Now, cigar, Ken?

1193
00:45:44,633 --> 00:45:45,900
- Yuck.

1194
00:45:45,900 --> 00:45:49,700
- You know, no sense in
me returning back home.

1195
00:45:49,700 --> 00:45:51,933
What with my wife
and child gone.

1196
00:45:51,933 --> 00:45:54,533
- Oh, that's right, they took
a laser bolt, didn't they?

1197
00:45:54,533 --> 00:45:55,367
Too bad.

1198
00:45:55,367 --> 00:45:56,667
- You know, cigar Ken?

1199
00:45:56,667 --> 00:45:58,367
You know, a young fellow?

1200
00:45:58,367 --> 00:46:00,567
I could use a few
of 'em on my ship.

1201
00:46:00,567 --> 00:46:02,733
A young fella could do a
lot worse than throw in

1202
00:46:02,733 --> 00:46:05,000
with the lot of Bacchus-3.

1203
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:06,800
We might even become friends.

1204
00:46:06,800 --> 00:46:09,467
- I don't understand, what
did I do to deserve this?

1205
00:46:09,467 --> 00:46:12,233
- We don't deserve
half the things we get.

1206
00:46:12,233 --> 00:46:14,333
(laughs)

1207
00:46:15,167 --> 00:46:16,433
You're stuck here!

1208
00:46:16,433 --> 00:46:18,767
- Gee, Joel, don't
vapor lock on us.

1209
00:46:18,767 --> 00:46:20,867
It's just a little skit
for cryin' out loud.

1210
00:46:20,867 --> 00:46:23,600
- Well, so I brought
the engines to neutral.

1211
00:46:23,600 --> 00:46:26,567
- Yeah, you do exactly as I
say and maybe you'll find out

1212
00:46:26,567 --> 00:46:29,300
what it means to be a
real man rather than just

1213
00:46:29,300 --> 00:46:30,767
a Wolf Raider.

1214
00:46:30,767 --> 00:46:33,100
- Yeah right, and you've
got a good chance to end up

1215
00:46:33,100 --> 00:46:34,900
at the Francis Farmer Motel.

1216
00:46:34,900 --> 00:46:36,200
(grunting)

1217
00:46:36,200 --> 00:46:37,467
- Jeez Joel, get a
hold of yourself!

1218
00:46:37,467 --> 00:46:39,333
- Nobody hits one
of my officers!

1219
00:46:39,333 --> 00:46:41,300
(alarms buzzing)

1220
00:46:41,300 --> 00:46:43,967
Oh no, the movie's starting, oh.

1221
00:46:54,000 --> 00:46:55,400
- [Tom] I think
you broke my jaw.

1222
00:46:55,400 --> 00:46:56,567
- [Joel] Sorry 'bout that.

1223
00:46:56,567 --> 00:46:58,833
- [Tom] Jeez, you're
outta control.

1224
00:46:58,833 --> 00:46:59,933
- [Crow] How symbolic.

1225
00:47:04,367 --> 00:47:05,733
- Are you on surveillance duty?

1226
00:47:05,733 --> 00:47:07,167
- Sorry I scared you.

1227
00:47:07,167 --> 00:47:09,400
You looked so angry I was afraid
I was gonna get strangled.

1228
00:47:09,400 --> 00:47:11,800
- [Tom] Well, there's
still time for that.

1229
00:47:11,800 --> 00:47:14,667
- Who's Rita, your wife
or your girlfriend?

1230
00:47:14,667 --> 00:47:16,000
- [All] Yes.

1231
00:47:16,000 --> 00:47:17,967
- Cat got your tongue?

1232
00:47:17,967 --> 00:47:18,800
- [Crow] Meow.

1233
00:47:18,800 --> 00:47:19,633
- Shut up!

1234
00:47:20,567 --> 00:47:22,100
Sorry, I'm just a little tired.

1235
00:47:22,100 --> 00:47:24,367
- You know Ken, I'm
beginning to think

1236
00:47:24,367 --> 00:47:26,233
you're not an earthling.

1237
00:47:26,233 --> 00:47:28,967
You haven't got the slightest
idea how to talk to a girl.

1238
00:47:28,967 --> 00:47:31,267
Honestly, I just
wanted to say hello.

1239
00:47:31,267 --> 00:47:32,967
You didn't have to
bite my head off.

1240
00:47:32,967 --> 00:47:33,900
- [Joel] Is that what I do?

1241
00:47:33,900 --> 00:47:36,067
- I don't feel like talking.

1242
00:47:36,067 --> 00:47:38,433
And I don't like people
meddling in my affairs.

1243
00:47:38,433 --> 00:47:39,600
- Oh, you don't?

1244
00:47:39,600 --> 00:47:40,933
Well have it your way.

1245
00:47:40,933 --> 00:47:42,133
- [Joel] At Burger King?

1246
00:47:44,600 --> 00:47:46,400
- [Narrator] This crew
had better start learning

1247
00:47:46,400 --> 00:47:49,500
to get along, it's gonna
be a difficult mission.

1248
00:47:50,933 --> 00:47:52,600
- [Joe] Our next mission
will take us to the Holy.

1249
00:47:52,600 --> 00:47:53,633
In the 32nd constellation

1250
00:47:53,633 --> 00:47:55,233
- [Tom] Holly Holy.

1251
00:47:55,233 --> 00:47:57,267
- However, before reaching
our final destination.

1252
00:47:57,267 --> 00:47:58,933
- [Joel] We all
get hats, big ones.

1253
00:47:58,933 --> 00:48:01,133
- [Tom] And scrambled eggs.

1254
00:48:01,133 --> 00:48:02,567
- Our assistance.

1255
00:48:02,567 --> 00:48:04,733
As you may have heard, Kararu
and Baholee are at war.

1256
00:48:04,733 --> 00:48:06,433
And recently the Wolf
Raiders have joined

1257
00:48:06,433 --> 00:48:07,833
forces with Baholee.

1258
00:48:08,933 --> 00:48:10,400
In other words,
this'll be no picnic.

1259
00:48:10,400 --> 00:48:11,700
- [Tom] More like a
small dinner party.

1260
00:48:11,700 --> 00:48:12,667
- Well, whatta
say, do we accept?

1261
00:48:12,667 --> 00:48:13,933
- [Tom] A buffet.

1262
00:48:13,933 --> 00:48:16,933
- Sir, I'd rather go and
fight than sit down here

1263
00:48:16,933 --> 00:48:18,433
bored out of my mind.

1264
00:48:18,433 --> 00:48:20,900
- Captain, I think this is
one mission where you're not

1265
00:48:20,900 --> 00:48:23,067
gonna need whiskey
for excitement.

1266
00:48:23,067 --> 00:48:24,333
(characters laughing)

1267
00:48:24,333 --> 00:48:25,900
- I'll need a stiff belt
when I get back though.

1268
00:48:25,900 --> 00:48:27,700
- [Crow] Ha, you'll
need a big belt.

1269
00:48:29,867 --> 00:48:31,100
- [Tom] I've got
baloney for arms!

1270
00:48:31,100 --> 00:48:32,500
- We're not gonna
take him along.

1271
00:48:32,500 --> 00:48:33,767
- [Joe] Cool it, Danny.

1272
00:48:33,767 --> 00:48:36,200
- But Captain, who is he?

1273
00:48:36,200 --> 00:48:38,600
- I've made my decision.
- What do we know about him?

1274
00:48:38,600 --> 00:48:40,633
- You can take it or leave it.

1275
00:48:40,633 --> 00:48:42,133
- [Tom] Well...

1276
00:48:42,133 --> 00:48:45,633
- Captain, I'm sorry, I'm sure
you know what you're doing.

1277
00:48:45,633 --> 00:48:47,800
- Captain, we accept
your decision.

1278
00:48:47,800 --> 00:48:49,267
Ken, welcome aboard.

1279
00:48:51,167 --> 00:48:52,900
- Are you sure you've got
what it takes for the job?

1280
00:48:52,900 --> 00:48:54,033
- You bet we have.

1281
00:48:54,033 --> 00:48:55,500
- [Tom] Don't press your luck.

1282
00:48:55,500 --> 00:48:57,133
- With Captain Joe in charge,
no mission is impossible.

1283
00:48:57,133 --> 00:48:59,333
- [Joe] Well, time will tell.

1284
00:48:59,333 --> 00:49:00,900
- [Crow] Monty
Python's Flying Circus.

1285
00:49:00,900 --> 00:49:03,600
- [Joel] Hey the crew got
free tanning sessions.

1286
00:49:03,600 --> 00:49:06,167
(upbeat music)

1287
00:49:06,167 --> 00:49:08,167
- [Crow] Pipe down,
pipe down please.

1288
00:49:08,167 --> 00:49:09,267
- [Joel] Pipe down please.

1289
00:49:09,267 --> 00:49:11,033
- [Tom] Pipe down please.

1290
00:49:12,200 --> 00:49:14,300
- All the way down here.

1291
00:49:14,300 --> 00:49:15,100
- [Crow] Now bite me please.

1292
00:49:15,100 --> 00:49:15,933
- [Joel] Hey.

1293
00:49:16,867 --> 00:49:18,267
(lively music)

1294
00:49:18,267 --> 00:49:19,700
- [Joel] What?

1295
00:49:19,700 --> 00:49:22,833
It's a good spaceship
in the cosmos.

1296
00:49:22,833 --> 00:49:24,300
- [Tom] What are Ma
and Pa Kettle goin'

1297
00:49:24,300 --> 00:49:25,400
on this mission or somethin'?

1298
00:49:25,400 --> 00:49:27,067
- [Crow] Hey there's Don Knotts.

1299
00:49:27,067 --> 00:49:28,800
(Joel laughing)

1300
00:49:28,800 --> 00:49:30,900
- [Joe] I've had her
rebuilt from stem to stern.

1301
00:49:30,900 --> 00:49:32,333
- [Tom] Neat huh?

1302
00:49:32,333 --> 00:49:33,900
- [Joe] To withstand the
extreme velocities out there.

1303
00:49:33,900 --> 00:49:35,333
I don't wanna have
another encounter

1304
00:49:35,333 --> 00:49:37,300
like I had with
the Wolf Raiders.

1305
00:49:37,300 --> 00:49:39,800
- [Rocky] I thought I was
gonna explode like a balloon.

1306
00:49:39,800 --> 00:49:41,000
- [Crow] Shouldn't have
had those buffalo wings.

1307
00:49:41,000 --> 00:49:42,233
- [Rocky] I sure hope
I never have to do

1308
00:49:42,233 --> 00:49:43,700
anything like that
again, Captain.

1309
00:49:43,700 --> 00:49:45,267
- [Billy] What are the
specs on this job, sir?

1310
00:49:45,267 --> 00:49:46,833
- [Joel] Oh, those are
bugs, they'll wash off.

1311
00:49:46,833 --> 00:49:48,467
- We've added a power
unit that can take us

1312
00:49:48,467 --> 00:49:51,067
up to speeds of
Mach 56 and over.

1313
00:49:51,067 --> 00:49:52,267
- [Crow] Yeah, pretty much.

1314
00:49:52,267 --> 00:49:53,300
- Any more speed
would tear us apart.

1315
00:49:53,300 --> 00:49:54,133
- [Crow] Yeah.

1316
00:49:54,133 --> 00:49:54,967
- You know.

1317
00:49:54,967 --> 00:49:56,467
- [Joel] Security guard?

1318
00:49:56,467 --> 00:49:57,267
- I'm really looking forward
to flying this old devil.

1319
00:49:57,267 --> 00:49:58,167
- So am I.

1320
00:49:58,167 --> 00:49:59,100
- Joe.
- Hi, Harry.

1321
00:49:59,100 --> 00:50:00,300
- [Tom] Hi teen gang.

1322
00:50:00,300 --> 00:50:02,567
- You really gonna
take on that mission?

1323
00:50:02,567 --> 00:50:03,700
- Sure thing.

1324
00:50:03,700 --> 00:50:05,633
- You leave the milk runs to us.

1325
00:50:05,633 --> 00:50:07,367
You always were a daredevil.

1326
00:50:07,367 --> 00:50:08,900
(chuckling)

1327
00:50:08,900 --> 00:50:11,333
By the way, is there
any truth to that rumor?

1328
00:50:11,333 --> 00:50:12,967
They say Rocky wants
out of this mission.

1329
00:50:12,967 --> 00:50:14,400
- [Tom] Come again?

1330
00:50:14,400 --> 00:50:16,933
- If he feels like a change,
I could sure use him.

1331
00:50:16,933 --> 00:50:19,233
- Sounds like someone's
overactive imagination.

1332
00:50:19,233 --> 00:50:22,133
Rocky's accounted
for, I wouldn't go
anywhere without him.

1333
00:50:22,133 --> 00:50:23,300
- Right on.

1334
00:50:23,300 --> 00:50:25,133
- [Crow] (laughs) You salty dog.

1335
00:50:25,133 --> 00:50:26,133
- Good luck.

1336
00:50:30,900 --> 00:50:32,500
- [Ken] This is a
strange development.

1337
00:50:32,500 --> 00:50:33,933
- [Tom] Wheels everywhere.

1338
00:50:33,933 --> 00:50:36,767
- [Ken] Using my superior
strength to fight my own people.

1339
00:50:36,767 --> 00:50:38,067
- [Crow] What is this,
The Wonder Years?

1340
00:50:38,067 --> 00:50:39,967
- [Ken] Sure I'd love
to liberate Valnastar

1341
00:50:39,967 --> 00:50:41,267
from the tyrant Halkun.
(imitating air hissing)

1342
00:50:41,267 --> 00:50:42,533
- [Tom] Lettin' the
air out of the tire.

1343
00:50:42,533 --> 00:50:44,333
- [Ken] My family's
up there and Rita.

1344
00:50:45,933 --> 00:50:48,133
Does she know I
killed her brother?

1345
00:50:48,133 --> 00:50:49,433
- [Joel] Maybe.

1346
00:50:49,433 --> 00:50:51,033
- [Ken] Will I ever be
able to explain to her

1347
00:50:51,033 --> 00:50:52,600
what really happened.

1348
00:50:52,600 --> 00:50:55,100
- [Tom] And what about
Naomi, will she love again?

1349
00:50:56,833 --> 00:50:57,967
- [Announcer] Is kindly
requested to report--

1350
00:50:59,300 --> 00:51:00,567
- [Joel] Trains, neat.

1351
00:51:00,567 --> 00:51:01,833
- [Tom] Cool, big ones.

1352
00:51:01,833 --> 00:51:02,767
- [Crow] Screamers.

1353
00:51:02,767 --> 00:51:04,900
- [Ken] That guy Rocky hates me.

1354
00:51:04,900 --> 00:51:07,000
Can Captain Joe control him?

1355
00:51:07,000 --> 00:51:07,833
- [Tom] Or not?

1356
00:51:08,967 --> 00:51:11,133
- [Crow] Will Joe admit
that Sue loves Mary?

1357
00:51:14,133 --> 00:51:15,400
(engine growling)

1358
00:51:15,400 --> 00:51:16,567
- [Joel] "Killdozer!"
with Clint Walker, no!

1359
00:51:16,567 --> 00:51:18,467
- Oh wow!
- Oh, oh no!

1360
00:51:20,867 --> 00:51:22,167
- [Crow] Eat fork, buddy.

1361
00:51:23,033 --> 00:51:24,567
- [Tom] He thinks I'm a palette.

1362
00:51:26,900 --> 00:51:28,167
- [Crow] Yeah well,
fortunate for me

1363
00:51:28,167 --> 00:51:30,733
I ate some more spinach
before I left the house.

1364
00:51:32,267 --> 00:51:35,933
- [Joel] Hey, come on, dim
your brights, I can't see!

1365
00:51:36,867 --> 00:51:38,900
(Tom grunting)

1366
00:51:38,900 --> 00:51:40,467
- [Tom] Oh, you should
know by now pal.

1367
00:51:40,467 --> 00:51:43,300
When you push a Wolf
Raider he pushes back.

1368
00:51:43,300 --> 00:51:46,333
(Tom chuckling)

1369
00:51:46,333 --> 00:51:48,167
(Tom grunting)

1370
00:51:48,167 --> 00:51:51,233
- [Crow] This must be one
of those Russian forklifts

1371
00:51:51,233 --> 00:51:54,233
I've heard so much about lately.

1372
00:51:56,400 --> 00:52:00,200
♪ This is the song written
for the train chase ♪

1373
00:52:00,200 --> 00:52:04,200
♪ This is chase Rocky and Ken ♪

1374
00:52:04,200 --> 00:52:08,067
♪ He tried to kill
me with a forklift ♪

1375
00:52:08,067 --> 00:52:10,733
♪ Ole ♪

1376
00:52:10,733 --> 00:52:12,133
- [Tom] Joe Mannix!

1377
00:52:12,133 --> 00:52:14,300
(singing)

1378
00:52:15,667 --> 00:52:16,800
- Rocky?

1379
00:52:16,800 --> 00:52:17,733
- [Crow] Again.

1380
00:52:17,733 --> 00:52:19,233
- Well that answers my question.

1381
00:52:19,233 --> 00:52:20,433
- [Tom] What was the question?

1382
00:52:20,433 --> 00:52:22,867
- I thought you
were a Wolf Raider.

1383
00:52:22,867 --> 00:52:25,267
They planted you on our flight
to sabotage our mission.

1384
00:52:25,267 --> 00:52:26,667
- [Joel] Yeah well,
you're a wuss raider.

1385
00:52:26,667 --> 00:52:29,600
(viewers giggling)

1386
00:52:31,967 --> 00:52:33,433
What are you doing,
are you high?

1387
00:52:33,433 --> 00:52:35,400
I have the strength of 20 men.

1388
00:52:35,400 --> 00:52:39,167
♪ This is the song right
after the train chase ♪

1389
00:52:39,167 --> 00:52:43,100
♪ This is the fight
Rocky and Ken ♪

1390
00:52:43,100 --> 00:52:43,933
- [Crow] Again?

1391
00:52:43,933 --> 00:52:45,300
- What's going on?

1392
00:52:45,300 --> 00:52:47,200
- [Joel] Nothing, sir.

1393
00:52:47,200 --> 00:52:48,133
- [Rocky] Captain!

1394
00:52:48,133 --> 00:52:49,400
- [Crow] Hazing the freshman.

1395
00:52:49,400 --> 00:52:52,233
- [Tom] I told you, no
grab-ass in the shower.

1396
00:52:52,233 --> 00:52:53,633
- I know who he is now.

1397
00:52:53,633 --> 00:52:55,367
- [Crow] He's my
mother, he's my sister.

1398
00:52:55,367 --> 00:52:56,967
He's my mother and my sister.

1399
00:52:58,233 --> 00:53:03,167
♪ He tried to kill
me with a forklift ♪

1400
00:53:04,333 --> 00:53:05,767
- Rocky, how often do
I have to tell you,

1401
00:53:05,767 --> 00:53:07,200
you should stop reading
those science fiction novels?

1402
00:53:07,200 --> 00:53:08,333
- [Crow] They're comic books.

1403
00:53:08,333 --> 00:53:09,800
- But captain?

1404
00:53:09,800 --> 00:53:12,133
- I know Ken's a lot
stronger than we are.

1405
00:53:12,133 --> 00:53:15,100
There's a reasonable scientific
explanation for that.

1406
00:53:15,100 --> 00:53:17,733
He spent a lot of time
in another constellation.

1407
00:53:17,733 --> 00:53:18,933
That increases strength.

1408
00:53:20,267 --> 00:53:21,400
- [Joel] You are a
liar, I don't believe,

1409
00:53:21,400 --> 00:53:22,533
you're just like him.

1410
00:53:25,800 --> 00:53:27,500
- [Ken] Don't expect
any gratitude from me.

1411
00:53:27,500 --> 00:53:29,000
- [Tom] Okay.

1412
00:53:29,000 --> 00:53:29,800
- I won't.

1413
00:53:31,533 --> 00:53:32,733
Now you listen to this.

1414
00:53:32,733 --> 00:53:34,000
- [Crow] Pull my finger.

1415
00:53:34,000 --> 00:53:36,633
- What I expect from
you is total obedience.

1416
00:53:36,633 --> 00:53:37,833
- [Tom] If that's okay with you.

1417
00:53:37,833 --> 00:53:39,867
- You know you'll
only continue to live

1418
00:53:39,867 --> 00:53:40,967
as long as I shut up.

1419
00:53:42,000 --> 00:53:44,733
(dramatic music)

1420
00:53:46,233 --> 00:53:50,867
♪ I got a threat
from the captain ♪

1421
00:53:50,867 --> 00:53:52,300
- [Joel] Shut up.

1422
00:53:53,200 --> 00:53:54,967
- [Crow] Wow.

1423
00:53:54,967 --> 00:53:56,667
- [Tom] Amazing!

1424
00:53:56,667 --> 00:53:57,467
Ooh, ah!

1425
00:53:59,533 --> 00:54:02,767
Ooh, gah, it's so great.

1426
00:54:02,767 --> 00:54:04,033
- [Crow] It's only a model.

1427
00:54:04,033 --> 00:54:05,600
- [Tom] All right, spit
out the sunflower seeds.

1428
00:54:05,600 --> 00:54:07,033
- [Narrator] And so, our
valiant space adventurers

1429
00:54:07,033 --> 00:54:09,900
prepared to embark on a
perilous and exciting mission.

1430
00:54:11,000 --> 00:54:13,300
- [Joel] Hold the
ship, lose the building

1431
00:54:13,300 --> 00:54:15,800
with Jerry Lewis, Charlie
Kalkenski, Franking!

1432
00:54:15,800 --> 00:54:17,033
(Tom humming tune)

1433
00:54:17,033 --> 00:54:19,267
- [Narrator] Meanwhile,
on Valnastar.

1434
00:54:19,267 --> 00:54:20,500
- [Tom] Say.

1435
00:54:20,500 --> 00:54:22,100
- [Announcer] Other
plans are being made.

1436
00:54:22,100 --> 00:54:24,367
- [Halkun] Remember
Rita, it is our law.

1437
00:54:24,367 --> 00:54:25,967
You may not return until--

1438
00:54:25,967 --> 00:54:27,000
- [Joel] Brian Jones?

1439
00:54:32,933 --> 00:54:35,200
- [Tom] Tell me spirit,
are these shadows

1440
00:54:35,200 --> 00:54:37,833
of things which must
be or which might be?

1441
00:54:39,133 --> 00:54:42,300
(birds chirping)

1442
00:54:42,300 --> 00:54:44,900
(Tom mumbling)

1443
00:54:48,233 --> 00:54:50,300
- [Tom] Hey look, 27 eight
by 10 colored glossy pictures

1444
00:54:50,300 --> 00:54:51,733
with the circles and
arrows and the paragraph

1445
00:54:51,733 --> 00:54:53,200
on the back of each one.

1446
00:54:53,200 --> 00:54:55,533
- [Crow] Why am I thinking
of the cast party now?

1447
00:54:55,533 --> 00:54:56,733
Oh, I like that one.

1448
00:54:59,867 --> 00:55:01,200
- Maryanne.

1449
00:55:01,200 --> 00:55:02,033
- [Joel] Uh, that'll be
53 bucks for the photos.

1450
00:55:02,033 --> 00:55:02,867
- Barbara.

1451
00:55:03,800 --> 00:55:05,600
- [Tom] Whose hand is that?

1452
00:55:05,600 --> 00:55:06,700
- [Crow] I can be Barbara.

1453
00:55:06,700 --> 00:55:08,533
- My baby, my wife.

1454
00:55:09,400 --> 00:55:10,600
- [Crow] Whatever.

1455
00:55:10,600 --> 00:55:11,667
- I don't care anymore
what happens to me

1456
00:55:11,667 --> 00:55:13,500
out beyond the stars.
- Ooh.

1457
00:55:14,933 --> 00:55:18,900
- If I don't survive, then
we can be together again

1458
00:55:18,900 --> 00:55:20,667
that much sooner.

1459
00:55:20,667 --> 00:55:23,367
- [Joel] Oh, would somebody
turn the fryer light off me.

1460
00:55:23,367 --> 00:55:24,200
- I miss you so.

1461
00:55:25,567 --> 00:55:28,600
Rest peacefully until
then, it won't be long now.

1462
00:55:29,633 --> 00:55:31,567
- [Tom] What a sap.

1463
00:55:31,567 --> 00:55:34,800
(soft music)

1464
00:55:34,800 --> 00:55:36,900
- [Joel] What, oh, I've got
the wrong grave, I'm sorry.

1465
00:55:36,900 --> 00:55:39,333
- [Crow] Olga, that is, whoops.

1466
00:55:40,333 --> 00:55:41,933
- [Tom] Oh, it's embarrassing.

1467
00:55:41,933 --> 00:55:44,700
- [Joel] I gotta go
paint a house now, sorry.

1468
00:55:44,700 --> 00:55:45,900
- Well, that just
about sums it all.

1469
00:55:45,900 --> 00:55:46,900
- [Crow] Hey they're
havin' a jumpsuit party

1470
00:55:46,900 --> 00:55:49,233
and his is the grandest of all.

1471
00:55:49,233 --> 00:55:51,567
- Thanks, you're a great crew.

1472
00:55:51,567 --> 00:55:53,400
- [Joel] Ready to
levitate the table?

1473
00:55:55,367 --> 00:55:56,467
- To the mission.

1474
00:55:56,467 --> 00:55:57,300
- [Crew] Cheers!

1475
00:55:58,700 --> 00:56:01,067
- [Tammy] Rocky, aren't
you going to drink with us?

1476
00:56:01,067 --> 00:56:02,700
- [Tom] Gonna fly now?

1477
00:56:02,700 --> 00:56:06,100
- Sir, I want you--

1478
00:56:06,100 --> 00:56:07,300
- [Joel] In the worst way.

1479
