01:04:54,967 --> 01:04:57,067
- [Joel] Eh, I'm not
a big fan either sir.

1724
01:04:58,200 --> 01:04:59,467
- Get lost.

1725
01:04:59,467 --> 01:05:00,733
- [Crow] You gotta
nice personality.

1726
01:05:00,733 --> 01:05:02,867
- [Patron] I guess
you're not from here.

1727
01:05:02,867 --> 01:05:04,800
Otherwise you'd know
it's good manners

1728
01:05:04,800 --> 01:05:07,033
to drink with friends, here.

1729
01:05:07,033 --> 01:05:09,033
- [Tom] I'd rather share a
needle with Keith Richards.

1730
01:05:09,033 --> 01:05:10,633
- I told you to drink!

1731
01:05:10,633 --> 01:05:13,300
- [Joel] Aw, Mom's
gonna smell this on me.

1732
01:05:13,300 --> 01:05:16,300
- [Ken] Doesn't he know I
can kill him with one blow?

1733
01:05:16,300 --> 01:05:17,700
- [Tom] Some ego, buddy.

1734
01:05:17,700 --> 01:05:19,567
- [Patron] Strangers
aren't welcome.

1735
01:05:19,567 --> 01:05:20,967
- [Crow] Gonna be a fight.

1736
01:05:20,967 --> 01:05:22,000
Fight, okay.

1737
01:05:22,000 --> 01:05:22,833
- Bye.

1738
01:05:24,067 --> 01:05:26,433
- [Patron] Hey,
where are you goin'?

1739
01:05:26,433 --> 01:05:28,200
- [Tom] Ooh, to
get a Band-Aid, ow!

1740
01:05:29,333 --> 01:05:30,267
My nose.

1741
01:05:30,267 --> 01:05:31,667
- [Patron] This will teach ya!

1742
01:05:31,667 --> 01:05:33,300
- [Crow] That's the problem
with private school.

1743
01:05:33,300 --> 01:05:34,867
- [Tom] Yeah,
yeah, you get this.

1744
01:05:36,067 --> 01:05:37,933
- [Joel] Ugh, thank you
sir, may I have another?

1745
01:05:39,567 --> 01:05:40,633
- [Tom] I like you guys.

1746
01:05:40,633 --> 01:05:42,100
- Here's one more.

1747
01:05:42,100 --> 01:05:44,567
- [Joel] Well, looks like
we've got three separate views

1748
01:05:44,567 --> 01:05:46,500
of Love, American Style.

1749
01:05:47,700 --> 01:05:49,600
- [Crow] Get up, get
up, get up, crunch,

1750
01:05:51,900 --> 01:05:53,500
Bam!

1751
01:05:53,500 --> 01:05:54,767
- [Tom] Buck!

1752
01:05:54,767 --> 01:05:56,233
- [Joel] Biff!

1753
01:05:56,233 --> 01:05:57,533
- [Crow] Bappy!

1754
01:05:57,533 --> 01:05:58,367
Eh, no.

1755
01:06:02,700 --> 01:06:05,700
♪ Lay down the boogie and
play that funky music ♪

1756
01:06:05,700 --> 01:06:08,533
♪ Till you die ♪

1757
01:06:08,533 --> 01:06:09,733
♪ Till you die ♪

1758
01:06:09,733 --> 01:06:12,700
- [Tom] Next on Taxi,
or Barney Miller.

1759
01:06:12,700 --> 01:06:14,467
One of the two.

1760
01:06:14,467 --> 01:06:15,733
- [Joel] What?

1761
01:06:15,733 --> 01:06:17,933
Oh, he killed him
with a curling iron.

1762
01:06:17,933 --> 01:06:18,767
Goodness.

1763
01:06:18,767 --> 01:06:19,833
- You're just...

1764
01:06:19,833 --> 01:06:20,733
- [Crow] A gigolo.

1765
01:06:21,933 --> 01:06:24,800
- Get him!
(gun fire ricocheting)

1766
01:06:24,800 --> 01:06:27,967
- [Joel] Yeah, get him, it's
his turn to buy the pitcher!

1767
01:06:28,867 --> 01:06:31,233
- [Patron] Stop him! (groaning)

1768
01:06:33,633 --> 01:06:36,200
(upbeat music)

1769
01:06:39,567 --> 01:06:40,800
- [Tom] Oh, he
stumbled back into

1770
01:06:40,800 --> 01:06:42,800
the Renaissance
Festival, huzzah.

1771
01:06:44,233 --> 01:06:48,733
♪ There's a place on Mars
where the women smoke cigars ♪

1772
01:06:48,733 --> 01:06:50,733
- [Joel] He looked in my
bag, I'll have to kill him.

1773
01:06:54,400 --> 01:06:55,233
- [Tom] Marian.

1774
01:06:56,367 --> 01:06:57,200
Oh, suddenly it is Ishtar here.

1775
01:06:57,200 --> 01:06:58,033
- In here!

1776
01:06:59,167 --> 01:06:59,833
- [Crow] Hey that's
a dressing room.

1777
01:06:59,833 --> 01:07:01,400
- Where is he?

1778
01:07:01,400 --> 01:07:03,067
- I saw him go in there.

1779
01:07:03,067 --> 01:07:04,733
- Come on!

1780
01:07:04,733 --> 01:07:05,567
- [Tom] Indy!

1781
01:07:07,000 --> 01:07:08,400
- [Joel] Oh, it's
a woman's restroom.

1782
01:07:08,400 --> 01:07:10,267
We can't go in there.

1783
01:07:10,267 --> 01:07:13,300
(mimicking snoring)

1784
01:07:13,300 --> 01:07:15,600
- [Joel] This is getting
ridiculous, you know?

1785
01:07:17,467 --> 01:07:18,633
- [Tom] Sir I think
you're losing them.

1786
01:07:18,633 --> 01:07:21,100
Tell a joke, juggle
or something.

1787
01:07:21,100 --> 01:07:23,467
- Just a second,
I'll be right back.

1788
01:07:25,200 --> 01:07:26,333
- [Joel] God, did you
say something to him

1789
01:07:26,333 --> 01:07:28,033
while I was
sleeping, what gives?

1790
01:07:30,800 --> 01:07:33,133
- [Crow] Hey look, it's
the all can network.

1791
01:07:33,133 --> 01:07:35,500
(dramatic music)

1792
01:07:35,500 --> 01:07:37,333
- Look who's in trouble.

1793
01:07:37,333 --> 01:07:38,800
What did he do?

1794
01:07:38,800 --> 01:07:40,633
- [Tom] Killed a man just
for snorin' too loud.

1795
01:07:42,000 --> 01:07:43,267
- [Crow] Who's ready
for pudding, huh?

1796
01:07:43,267 --> 01:07:45,633
- Was in the space craft
during our negotiations.

1797
01:07:45,633 --> 01:07:48,400
That man was arrested in a
storehouse for precious stones.

1798
01:07:48,400 --> 01:07:49,333
- [Tom] Arrested?

1799
01:07:49,333 --> 01:07:50,700
- What was he doing in there?

1800
01:07:50,700 --> 01:07:52,500
- [Joe] Your excellency,
if he left the ship

1801
01:07:52,500 --> 01:07:54,633
it was in direct
violation of my orders.

1802
01:07:54,633 --> 01:07:57,233
- You ordered him
to steal the stones.

1803
01:07:57,233 --> 01:07:58,967
- [Tom] Oh, thanks
for spitting on us.

1804
01:07:58,967 --> 01:08:00,567
- [Joel] This guy's a king?

1805
01:08:00,567 --> 01:08:02,400
- I'm afraid he doesn't
take orders seriously.

1806
01:08:02,400 --> 01:08:03,933
- I ordered him to stay aboard.

1807
01:08:03,933 --> 01:08:06,800
- Then you don't mind
if I cut off his head?

1808
01:08:06,800 --> 01:08:08,000
- [Crow] No, that's
why we brought him.

1809
01:08:08,000 --> 01:08:09,667
- Not at all, suit yourself.

1810
01:08:11,767 --> 01:08:13,267
- [Joel] I tire of pudding.

1811
01:08:13,267 --> 01:08:14,067
Bring me something salty,
and crunchy, and sweet.

1812
01:08:14,067 --> 01:08:15,767
- Order the execution.

1813
01:08:16,700 --> 01:08:17,533
Where were we?

1814
01:08:17,533 --> 01:08:18,467
- [Crow] Goofy land.

1815
01:08:18,467 --> 01:08:22,200
- We were discussing the fee.

1816
01:08:22,200 --> 01:08:23,000
- That's right.

1817
01:08:23,000 --> 01:08:24,267
- [Tom] Ah, yes.

1818
01:08:24,267 --> 01:08:25,700
- Let me give you
your down payment.

1819
01:08:25,700 --> 01:08:26,733
- [Tom] My little bag.

1820
01:08:26,733 --> 01:08:27,567
- One.

1821
01:08:27,567 --> 01:08:28,400
- [Tom] Little.

1822
01:08:28,400 --> 01:08:29,233
- Two.

1823
01:08:29,233 --> 01:08:30,633
- [Tom] Little.

1824
01:08:30,633 --> 01:08:31,767
- Three.

1825
01:08:31,767 --> 01:08:32,900
- [Tom] Little Indians,
I love that one.

1826
01:08:32,900 --> 01:08:33,700
- Three!

1827
01:08:34,667 --> 01:08:36,400
(laughing)

1828
01:08:36,400 --> 01:08:38,400
- [Tom] It's Jimmy Cow Black,
the Indian in the group.

1829
01:08:38,400 --> 01:08:40,033
- [Joel] Milk from
the mother stone.

1830
01:08:40,033 --> 01:08:41,433
Snot's block?

1831
01:08:43,767 --> 01:08:46,333
- We'll collect the
rest on completion.

1832
01:08:46,333 --> 01:08:48,000
- [Crow] Of the Brooklyn Bridge?

1833
01:08:48,000 --> 01:08:50,767
- [Tom] Hey, Sonny
Rollins is out there.

1834
01:08:50,767 --> 01:08:53,667
- [Joel] Hey, my helmet's
chafing, Steve, you?

1835
01:08:53,667 --> 01:08:55,133
- [Crow] Igor,
quit playing that.

1836
01:08:55,133 --> 01:08:57,400
(tense music)

1837
01:08:57,400 --> 01:08:58,500
- [Tom] Sure is quiet.

1838
01:08:59,500 --> 01:09:00,367
Too quiet.

1839
01:09:03,600 --> 01:09:07,167
- [Crow] That oboe's
comin' from that room.

1840
01:09:09,333 --> 01:09:11,733
- [Tom] It's the Rite
of Spring, Stravinsky?

1841
01:09:11,733 --> 01:09:13,400
They let him have a
chamber group in his cell?

1842
01:09:13,400 --> 01:09:15,300
- [Crow] No, a chamber pot.

1843
01:09:15,300 --> 01:09:16,933
- [Tom] Oh.

1844
01:09:16,933 --> 01:09:18,167
Musical pot.

1845
01:09:18,167 --> 01:09:20,400
- [Joel] Thanks for the
little prelude, guys.

1846
01:09:22,733 --> 01:09:26,733
I've got a crazy Star Wolf
idea that just might work.

1847
01:09:26,733 --> 01:09:29,133
(grunting)

1848
01:09:29,133 --> 01:09:31,400
- [Crow] His Mickey Mouse gloves
give him incredible power.

1849
01:09:31,400 --> 01:09:33,267
- [Tom] That's a
trademark of whatever.

1850
01:09:34,433 --> 01:09:36,833
(metal clanging)

1851
01:09:36,833 --> 01:09:37,933
Huh?

1852
01:09:37,933 --> 01:09:38,767
Hmm.

1853
01:09:39,867 --> 01:09:44,867
Hmm, hmm, hmm.

1854
01:09:45,600 --> 01:09:46,833
- [Joel] Spider-Man.

1855
01:09:46,833 --> 01:09:48,333
- [Crow] Yeah but not
the new Spider-Man,

1856
01:09:48,333 --> 01:09:49,200
the old Spider-Man when he had
the good costume and when--

1857
01:09:49,200 --> 01:09:50,033
- [Tom] Ssh.

1858
01:09:50,033 --> 01:09:50,867
- [Crow] Oh.

1859
01:09:50,867 --> 01:09:51,700
- [Tom] Huh?

1860
01:09:53,167 --> 01:09:55,900
- [Crow] Oh great, first
day on the job I lose a guy.

1861
01:10:00,433 --> 01:10:01,433
Ah?

1862
01:10:01,433 --> 01:10:03,133
- Come on, get down!

1863
01:10:03,133 --> 01:10:04,600
This is no monkey cage.

1864
01:10:04,600 --> 01:10:07,233
- [Joel] This is no disco,
this ain't no fooling around.

1865
01:10:07,233 --> 01:10:08,467
(Ken laughing)

1866
01:10:08,467 --> 01:10:09,867
- I was just checking
out the layout here.

1867
01:10:09,867 --> 01:10:11,500
- [Joel] The cool
moldings, you have a couple

1868
01:10:11,500 --> 01:10:12,333
cobwebs and stuff.

1869
01:10:12,333 --> 01:10:13,533
- I can't find the exit.

1870
01:10:13,533 --> 01:10:14,800
If I can't find
one, I'll make one.

1871
01:10:14,800 --> 01:10:16,467
- Cut the funny stuff.

1872
01:10:16,467 --> 01:10:17,967
You've just been
ordered executed.

1873
01:10:17,967 --> 01:10:19,700
That oughta take the
smile off your face.

1874
01:10:19,700 --> 01:10:20,933
- [Crow] Not if you do it right.

1875
01:10:20,933 --> 01:10:23,400
- By the way, don't
waste your energy.

1876
01:10:23,400 --> 01:10:25,267
You can't get outta here.

1877
01:10:25,267 --> 01:10:26,233
No earthling can.

1878
01:10:26,233 --> 01:10:27,667
- Earthling?

1879
01:10:27,667 --> 01:10:29,700
- Not even a Wolf Raider
could break out of this place.

1880
01:10:29,700 --> 01:10:31,033
- Is that so?

1881
01:10:31,033 --> 01:10:32,467
We'll see about that!

1882
01:10:32,467 --> 01:10:34,533
- [Tom] Meanwhile
back at the cool ship.

1883
01:10:36,733 --> 01:10:38,767
- Captain, anyone
can make a mistake.

1884
01:10:40,200 --> 01:10:42,333
Just as long as you don't
keep on repeating it.

1885
01:10:42,333 --> 01:10:44,267
I think we should
get rid of Ken.

1886
01:10:44,267 --> 01:10:45,133
- [Tom] Which one?

1887
01:10:45,133 --> 01:10:46,000
- I disagree.

1888
01:10:46,900 --> 01:10:48,233
Have you already forgotten?

1889
01:10:49,733 --> 01:10:52,400
Ken saved our lives, I think
he deserves another chance.

1890
01:10:52,400 --> 01:10:54,600
Don't you agree?

1891
01:10:54,600 --> 01:10:55,567
- Okay.

1892
01:10:55,567 --> 01:10:56,533
- [Tom] Man of firm conviction.

1893
01:10:56,533 --> 01:10:57,633
- I guess you're right.

1894
01:10:58,867 --> 01:11:00,567
I'll take him back
on one condition.

1895
01:11:00,567 --> 01:11:02,933
- [Joel] You stop drinking
and start going to meetings.

1896
01:11:02,933 --> 01:11:05,267
- There's a Caesar
officer in that jail.

1897
01:11:05,267 --> 01:11:06,100
- Mm.

1898
01:11:06,100 --> 01:11:07,367
- [Tom] Mm.

1899
01:11:07,367 --> 01:11:09,167
- You think Ken can help
him break out of there.

1900
01:11:09,167 --> 01:11:10,700
- Let's go to it.

1901
01:11:10,700 --> 01:11:12,833
Establish contact with Ken's
secret radio, on the double!

1902
01:11:12,833 --> 01:11:14,267
- [Crow] No you guys go ahead.

1903
01:11:14,267 --> 01:11:17,367
I'm sick, I'll just stay
here and not go through that.

1904
01:11:18,300 --> 01:11:19,933
- [Tom] I wish I
had a harmonica.

1905
01:11:19,933 --> 01:11:21,067
(beeping)

1906
01:11:21,067 --> 01:11:21,900
- Hmm?

1907
01:11:23,667 --> 01:11:25,333
- [Crow] Cleveland
you're on the air.

1908
01:11:25,333 --> 01:11:27,233
- [Joe] Ken, can you hear me?

1909
01:11:28,167 --> 01:11:29,333
It's me, Joe.

1910
01:11:29,333 --> 01:11:30,600
- [Joel] Yeah, I
really miss you, dude.

1911
01:11:30,600 --> 01:11:31,733
We haven't talked
since high school.

1912
01:11:31,733 --> 01:11:33,233
What's goin' on?

1913
01:11:33,233 --> 01:11:34,467
- You never told me about
this cute little gadget.

1914
01:11:34,467 --> 01:11:35,933
- [Joe] You don't have
to know everything.

1915
01:11:35,933 --> 01:11:37,200
- [Tom] What's romance
without a little surprise?

1916
01:11:37,200 --> 01:11:38,133
- [Joe] We wanted to
wanted to make sure

1917
01:11:38,133 --> 01:11:39,600
you wouldn't double-cross us.

1918
01:11:39,600 --> 01:11:41,900
- And I guess I passed your
examination, haven't I?

1919
01:11:41,900 --> 01:11:42,900
Now what do you want me to do?

1920
01:11:42,900 --> 01:11:44,300
- [Joe] Listen carefully.

1921
01:11:44,300 --> 01:11:45,567
- [Tom] Turn your
head and cough.

1922
01:11:45,567 --> 01:11:49,500
- Ken, there's a Caesar
officer in your jail.

1923
01:11:49,500 --> 01:11:52,233
We need him as camouflage
when we move onto Caesar.

1924
01:11:52,233 --> 01:11:53,933
They won't suspect
anything if we show up

1925
01:11:53,933 --> 01:11:55,267
with one of their officers.

1926
01:11:56,467 --> 01:11:58,800
We want you to
contact that officer.

1927
01:11:58,800 --> 01:12:00,633
Get him and yourself
out of prison.

1928
01:12:00,633 --> 01:12:02,567
- Why don't you just ask
the Kararun authorities

1929
01:12:02,567 --> 01:12:04,067
to release us?

1930
01:12:04,067 --> 01:12:05,267
- [Crow] Well, if you're so
smart why are you in jail?

1931
01:12:05,267 --> 01:12:07,333
- [Joe] Five minutes
and they got suspicious.

1932
01:12:08,833 --> 01:12:11,467
If I say I wanna
take him to Caesar,

1933
01:12:11,467 --> 01:12:13,700
chances are they'll
think I joined forces

1934
01:12:13,700 --> 01:12:15,167
with their mortal enemies.

1935
01:12:15,167 --> 01:12:16,767
- Are you sure I can
find him and get him

1936
01:12:16,767 --> 01:12:18,167
out of this prison?

1937
01:12:18,167 --> 01:12:19,833
- [Joe] Sure Ken, I
have complete confidence

1938
01:12:19,833 --> 01:12:20,667
you can bring it off.

1939
01:12:20,667 --> 01:12:21,600
- Ssh, somebody coming.

1940
01:12:21,600 --> 01:12:23,067
- [Joel] 'Course I'm drunk.

1941
01:12:23,067 --> 01:12:24,033
- [Tom] And I'm sure
the other inmates

1942
01:12:24,033 --> 01:12:26,233
haven't heard a word of this.

1943
01:12:26,233 --> 01:12:29,133
(mimicking snoring)

1944
01:12:29,133 --> 01:12:32,200
♪ Hmm hmm hmm we're
just sleeping ♪

1945
01:12:32,200 --> 01:12:33,567
(Joel chuckling)

1946
01:12:33,567 --> 01:12:35,600
- [Joel] Works every time.

1947
01:12:35,600 --> 01:12:37,500
- He's gone now.

1948
01:12:37,500 --> 01:12:41,033
Listen sir, aren't the
Kararuns likely to suspect you

1949
01:12:41,033 --> 01:12:42,433
if I break out of here?

1950
01:12:42,433 --> 01:12:44,133
- The Kararuns can
suspect anything they want

1951
01:12:44,133 --> 01:12:45,533
as long as I can
get off this planet.

1952
01:12:45,533 --> 01:12:47,400
- [Crow] And he's got
the generous cheeks.

1953
01:12:47,400 --> 01:12:48,900
- I understand.

1954
01:12:48,900 --> 01:12:52,100
Only, how am I supposed to
get out of this prison cell?

1955
01:12:53,300 --> 01:12:56,100
Those bars are as
strong as tree trunks.

1956
01:12:56,100 --> 01:12:57,467
- [Tom] Here's how I escape.

1957
01:12:59,033 --> 01:13:01,633
- Is Star Wolf
suddenly going soft?

1958
01:13:01,633 --> 01:13:02,867
- Just give me my orders.

1959
01:13:02,867 --> 01:13:04,400
- [Tom] Soft wolf.

1960
01:13:04,400 --> 01:13:06,300
- You'll find you've got some
clever little items with you.

1961
01:13:06,300 --> 01:13:07,933
- Go on.

1962
01:13:07,933 --> 01:13:10,233
- Okay, I want you
to listen carefully.

1963
01:13:10,233 --> 01:13:11,667
- [Joel] All right, I'm
using a split screen.

1964
01:13:11,667 --> 01:13:12,900
Can you see me now?

1965
01:13:12,900 --> 01:13:14,367
- [Crow] It's the
Patty Duke show.

1966
01:13:14,367 --> 01:13:17,433
- Now take a good look at your
far right shoulder button.

1967
01:13:17,433 --> 01:13:18,867
