01:22:54,833 --> 01:22:55,800
- You really picked
those two off easily.

2212
01:22:55,800 --> 01:22:57,800
- Well, I'm not a bad shot.

2213
01:22:57,800 --> 01:22:59,067
Watch this.

2214
01:22:59,067 --> 01:23:00,733
- [Tom] Oh, that
was a thrill kill.

2215
01:23:00,733 --> 01:23:01,700
(alarm beeping)

2216
01:23:01,700 --> 01:23:03,567
- [Crow] Duck alarm, run.

2217
01:23:03,567 --> 01:23:05,433
- [Joel] Oh, we got an
extra point on that.

2218
01:23:06,400 --> 01:23:08,167
(dramatic music)

2219
01:23:08,167 --> 01:23:09,000
- This way.

2220
01:23:09,867 --> 01:23:12,433
(upbeat music)

2221
01:23:19,800 --> 01:23:20,967
- [Officer] Water!

2222
01:23:20,967 --> 01:23:23,500
- Careful, it
might be an ambush.

2223
01:23:25,800 --> 01:23:28,533
- [Crow] Wait a minute, it
tastes salty, it's grey water!

2224
01:23:28,533 --> 01:23:30,800
(grunting)

2225
01:23:32,200 --> 01:23:33,133
- [Ken] Ah!

2226
01:23:35,133 --> 01:23:36,633
- [Tom] Delicious.

2227
01:23:37,833 --> 01:23:38,667
Huh?

2228
01:23:38,667 --> 01:23:40,067
- There they are.

2229
01:23:41,500 --> 01:23:42,400
(weapons firing)

2230
01:23:42,400 --> 01:23:43,400
- [Tom] Ooh.

2231
01:23:46,500 --> 01:23:47,333
Ah.

2232
01:23:50,633 --> 01:23:52,033
Terrible violence.

2233
01:23:52,033 --> 01:23:53,267
- [Joel] Terrible.

2234
01:23:53,267 --> 01:23:54,433
- [Tom] Oh, they're
only shooting flares.

2235
01:23:54,433 --> 01:23:55,233
- [Crow] I think
they're talcum bombs.

2236
01:23:55,233 --> 01:23:56,933
- [Tom] Yeah, could be.

2237
01:23:57,933 --> 01:23:58,867
Huh?

2238
01:23:58,867 --> 01:24:00,433
Huh?

2239
01:24:00,433 --> 01:24:02,067
- [Joel] Die, Joel.

2240
01:24:02,067 --> 01:24:03,000
- [Tom] Huh?

2241
01:24:03,000 --> 01:24:03,867
- [Tom] Button bombs, whoa!

2242
01:24:03,867 --> 01:24:04,767
- [All] Ah!

2243
01:24:06,600 --> 01:24:08,800
- [Crow] Hey wow, those
things really work.

2244
01:24:08,800 --> 01:24:10,100
- [Joel] You gotta
remember to take them off

2245
01:24:10,100 --> 01:24:11,967
before you take your
clothes to the laundry.

2246
01:24:11,967 --> 01:24:13,200
- [Crow] Oh, yeah.

2247
01:24:13,200 --> 01:24:15,000
- [Tom] Blow up a dry cleaner.

2248
01:24:15,000 --> 01:24:17,567
Oh, this was a good
plan, wasn't it?

2249
01:24:21,400 --> 01:24:22,233
Whoops.

2250
01:24:23,433 --> 01:24:25,767
All right, come on
in, bring her down.

2251
01:24:25,767 --> 01:24:27,000
Little right, little right.

2252
01:24:27,000 --> 01:24:28,767
Up there you go, watch
your space cushion.

2253
01:24:28,767 --> 01:24:30,633
It's a little driving joke.

2254
01:24:30,633 --> 01:24:32,767
Bring it down, keep
going, come on, come on.

2255
01:24:32,767 --> 01:24:34,300
- [Crow] No, I'm sorry
you failed your test.

2256
01:24:34,300 --> 01:24:35,900
You'll have to come
back in two weeks.

2257
01:24:35,900 --> 01:24:37,400
Happens to most of the guys.

2258
01:24:39,667 --> 01:24:40,900
- This is Joe.

2259
01:24:40,900 --> 01:24:42,133
- [Joel] Hello Joe,
what do you know?

2260
01:24:42,133 --> 01:24:43,367
- [Tom] Just got
back from Kokomo.

2261
01:24:43,367 --> 01:24:44,633
(laughing)

2262
01:24:44,633 --> 01:24:45,933
- You surprised me
of your position.

2263
01:24:45,933 --> 01:24:46,767
Ken?

2264
01:24:46,767 --> 01:24:48,000
- [Tom] Ken?

2265
01:24:48,000 --> 01:24:49,467
- Can you hear me,
Ken, please come in.

2266
01:24:49,467 --> 01:24:51,267
(soft music)

2267
01:24:51,267 --> 01:24:52,900
- [Tom] Ready?

2268
01:24:52,900 --> 01:24:57,333
♪ I love Ken and a guy named
Ken and it hurts me so ♪

2269
01:24:57,333 --> 01:25:00,733
♪ I'm in love Ken and a guy
named Ken and it hurts me so ♪

2270
01:25:00,733 --> 01:25:05,733
♪ I'm in love Ken and a guy
named Ken and it hurts me so ♪

2271
01:25:06,500 --> 01:25:07,733
♪ And it hurts me so ♪

2272
01:25:07,733 --> 01:25:10,833
♪ And it hurts me so ♪

2273
01:25:11,933 --> 01:25:13,200
- [Joel] Moses?

2274
01:25:13,200 --> 01:25:14,700
- [Ken] Arita.

2275
01:25:14,700 --> 01:25:16,800
- [Crow] Meter maid, where
would I be without you.

2276
01:25:16,800 --> 01:25:18,200
- I'm seeing things.

2277
01:25:18,200 --> 01:25:19,433
- [Joel] No, you're seeing me.

2278
01:25:19,433 --> 01:25:21,367
Is that what I am
to you, a thing?

2279
01:25:21,367 --> 01:25:22,233
- This must be a hallucination.

2280
01:25:23,400 --> 01:25:25,100
- [Crow] With that
hair it must be.

2281
01:25:26,700 --> 01:25:28,067
- Rita!

2282
01:25:28,067 --> 01:25:29,400
What are you doing here?

2283
01:25:29,400 --> 01:25:31,733
- I've been trying to
track you down for days.

2284
01:25:31,733 --> 01:25:33,933
We got a radio message
that you'd broken out

2285
01:25:33,933 --> 01:25:35,133
of a Kararu jail.

2286
01:25:36,500 --> 01:25:38,600
They said you were a traitor.

2287
01:25:38,600 --> 01:25:41,300
And here you are in an
Earth Space Command uniform.

2288
01:25:41,300 --> 01:25:42,567
- [Tom] Traiting.

2289
01:25:42,567 --> 01:25:44,567
- I was forced to
wear this uniform.

2290
01:25:44,567 --> 01:25:45,933
They said they'd
kill me otherwise.

2291
01:25:45,933 --> 01:25:48,067
- Mm hm.
- A likely story.

2292
01:25:48,067 --> 01:25:49,900
I don't know what's
come over you, Ken.

2293
01:25:49,900 --> 01:25:51,533
- [Crow] I want my tapes back.

2294
01:25:51,533 --> 01:25:54,533
- You've turned
traitor, abandoned me
and killed my brother.

2295
01:25:54,533 --> 01:25:55,767
- It was an accident.

2296
01:25:55,767 --> 01:25:57,033
- [Tom] Okay.

2297
01:25:57,033 --> 01:25:58,500
- He was getting ready
to shoot a little boy

2298
01:25:58,500 --> 01:26:00,433
whose name also
happened to be Ken.

2299
01:26:00,433 --> 01:26:02,000
I was just trying to stop him.

2300
01:26:02,000 --> 01:26:02,833
- [Woman] Ken!

2301
01:26:02,833 --> 01:26:04,100
- Mom!

2302
01:26:04,100 --> 01:26:04,567
- [Tom] But we'll
just run the clip.

2303
01:26:05,767 --> 01:26:07,133
- Don't shoot!

2304
01:26:07,133 --> 01:26:08,600
(groaning)

2305
01:26:08,600 --> 01:26:10,433
- [Crow] Oh, come on, we're
intimate with this scene

2306
01:26:10,433 --> 01:26:11,267
for crying out loud.

2307
01:26:11,267 --> 01:26:12,100
- Traitor.

2308
01:26:13,233 --> 01:26:14,667
- That's what really
happened, Rita.

2309
01:26:14,667 --> 01:26:16,800
I swear I'm telling
you the truth.

2310
01:26:16,800 --> 01:26:18,833
I'm not a traitor
to our country.

2311
01:26:18,833 --> 01:26:22,167
You know that, I simply refused
to kill an innocent child.

2312
01:26:23,300 --> 01:26:24,967
And I didn't want to
fight with your brother!

2313
01:26:24,967 --> 01:26:25,967
- [Joel] So I killed him.

2314
01:26:25,967 --> 01:26:27,467
- [Rita] I believe you.

2315
01:26:27,467 --> 01:26:29,800
You can't betray a country
you never belonged to.

2316
01:26:29,800 --> 01:26:31,333
- [Tom] Hmm?

2317
01:26:31,333 --> 01:26:32,733
- [Rita] Ken, you once told
me your father came to Valna

2318
01:26:32,733 --> 01:26:34,000
as a missionary.

2319
01:26:34,000 --> 01:26:34,800
- [Tom] Oh, that bag,
I thought they cleared

2320
01:26:34,800 --> 01:26:36,000
that up in counseling.

2321
01:26:36,000 --> 01:26:37,500
- [Rita] You're
really an earthling.

2322
01:26:37,500 --> 01:26:40,600
- Go on, go on, murder me in
cold blood if you want to.

2323
01:26:40,600 --> 01:26:43,333
- You deserve worse,
to die a slow death.

2324
01:26:43,333 --> 01:26:44,600
- Then what are you waiting for?

2325
01:26:44,600 --> 01:26:46,800
I know Valna law
as well as you do.

2326
01:26:46,800 --> 01:26:48,967
I caused your brother's
death and now you've been

2327
01:26:48,967 --> 01:26:50,667
sent out to kill me.

2328
01:26:50,667 --> 01:26:53,067
Well I'm all ready to die, Rita.

2329
01:26:53,067 --> 01:26:54,567
- Ken...

2330
01:26:54,567 --> 01:26:58,300
- You'd be doing me a favor,
I can't live in dishonor.

2331
01:26:58,300 --> 01:26:59,967
Go ahead, shoot!

2332
01:26:59,967 --> 01:27:02,867
- [Crow] But first,
swallow my lapel button

2333
01:27:02,867 --> 01:27:04,967
as a symbol of our love, hmm?

2334
01:27:04,967 --> 01:27:07,600
- [Tom] Shoot him
down, shoot to kill.

2335
01:27:07,600 --> 01:27:08,967
- [Joel] Stinker.

2336
01:27:10,833 --> 01:27:11,767
- [Tom] Buck fever.

2337
01:27:13,500 --> 01:27:15,967
Oh, it's made out of
electrician's tape,

2338
01:27:15,967 --> 01:27:17,200
for crying out loud.

2339
01:27:17,200 --> 01:27:18,633
- [Ken] Come on,
get it over with.

2340
01:27:18,633 --> 01:27:20,100
What's the point of
living if the girl I love

2341
01:27:20,100 --> 01:27:22,600
more than life itself
thinks that I'm a traitor?

2342
01:27:22,600 --> 01:27:23,433
- [Joel] Kill him.

2343
01:27:23,433 --> 01:27:24,267
- [Tom] Kill him.

2344
01:27:24,267 --> 01:27:25,500
- Now, Rita.

2345
01:27:25,500 --> 01:27:26,933
- [Tom] Now.

2346
01:27:26,933 --> 01:27:29,033
- [Crow] Hey, this is
just like Richard III.

2347
01:27:29,033 --> 01:27:29,867
- [Tom] Sure is.

2348
01:27:31,167 --> 01:27:32,100
(Rita sobbing)

2349
01:27:32,100 --> 01:27:33,567
Won't do it.

2350
01:27:33,567 --> 01:27:34,400
- [Joel] It took me seven
days to get this gun,

2351
01:27:34,400 --> 01:27:35,267
now I can't use it.

2352
01:27:35,267 --> 01:27:36,333
- [Ken] Rita!

2353
01:27:37,533 --> 01:27:38,633
- [Tom] Damn.

2354
01:27:40,000 --> 01:27:42,300
Nice to see there was a
dam in the background.

2355
01:27:43,667 --> 01:27:45,667
- [Joel] That peasant
blouse is all wrong on her.

2356
01:27:45,667 --> 01:27:46,500
- Rita.

2357
01:27:47,833 --> 01:27:50,900
- I can't do it, I can't
kill the man I love.

2358
01:27:50,900 --> 01:27:52,667
- [Crow] Then kill
the one you're with.

2359
01:27:55,367 --> 01:27:56,867
(Tom mimicking gunshot)

2360
01:27:56,867 --> 01:27:59,767
- Oh, my foot, why am I
having such a crappy day?

2361
01:28:00,767 --> 01:28:01,600
- Rita.

2362
01:28:01,600 --> 01:28:03,133
- [All] Meter maid.

2363
01:28:06,633 --> 01:28:08,133
- [Tom] There's that
glycerin tear again.

2364
01:28:08,133 --> 01:28:09,200
- My darling.

2365
01:28:10,500 --> 01:28:11,333
Ken.

2366
01:28:12,533 --> 01:28:13,500
- [Tom] I'm gonna have
to remember that line

2367
01:28:13,500 --> 01:28:15,233
for the bars, it works.

2368
01:28:15,233 --> 01:28:17,267
(sobbing)

2369
01:28:17,267 --> 01:28:19,100
- [Crow] You're
crying on my bomb.

2370
01:28:19,100 --> 01:28:20,733
- [Tom] Ooh.

2371
01:28:20,733 --> 01:28:21,567
Ouch.

2372
01:28:23,533 --> 01:28:24,933
- [Ken] Rita!

2373
01:28:24,933 --> 01:28:28,867
- [Joel] Oh, get off
the tilt-a-whirl.

2374
01:28:28,867 --> 01:28:31,100
- [Tom] Ooh, oh, it's over.

2375
01:28:32,067 --> 01:28:33,400
- [Crow] That was great.

2376
01:28:33,400 --> 01:28:34,600
- What happens to us now?

2377
01:28:34,600 --> 01:28:36,200
Are we both just
fugitives in space?

2378
01:28:37,367 --> 01:28:38,967
No matter what you
or I say or do,

2379
01:28:38,967 --> 01:28:40,933
they'll never let us go home.

2380
01:28:40,933 --> 01:28:43,700
Valna, I'd love to see it again.

2381
01:28:43,700 --> 01:28:46,700
- What do we need Valna
for, we've got each other.

2382
01:28:46,700 --> 01:28:48,600
We can start a new
life somewhere else.

2383
01:28:48,600 --> 01:28:49,433
- [Tom] On a slag heap?

2384
01:28:49,433 --> 01:28:51,033
- Rita, it won't work.

2385
01:28:52,200 --> 01:28:53,933
They'll never leave us
in peace, you know that.

2386
01:28:53,933 --> 01:28:55,233
- How can you say that?

2387
01:28:56,600 --> 01:28:59,533
If we keep loving each
other, we'll find a way.

2388
01:28:59,533 --> 01:29:00,533
- [Joel] Boy you are naive.

2389
01:29:00,533 --> 01:29:02,100
- How long can that love last?

2390
01:29:02,100 --> 01:29:04,633
You know what you'll see every
morning when you wake up?

2391
01:29:04,633 --> 01:29:06,200
You'll be staring
straight at the man

2392
01:29:06,200 --> 01:29:07,200
who killed your brother.

2393
01:29:07,200 --> 01:29:08,233
- [Crow] Will you be there too?

2394
01:29:08,233 --> 01:29:09,700
- Ken.

2395
01:29:09,700 --> 01:29:13,133
- It won't work, Rita, too much
has already happened to us.

2396
01:29:13,133 --> 01:29:15,300
Soon we'd start
hating each other.

2397
01:29:15,300 --> 01:29:16,800
- I won't let you
talk like that.

2398
01:29:16,800 --> 01:29:18,333
- It just won't work.

2399
01:29:18,333 --> 01:29:19,633
Why didn't you kill me before?

2400
01:29:19,633 --> 01:29:20,467
- Oh!
- What?

2401
01:29:21,633 --> 01:29:24,100
- You heard, kill me
and get it over with.

2402
01:29:24,100 --> 01:29:26,267
- [Tom] Come on chicken, you
chicken, come on kill me,

2403
01:29:26,267 --> 01:29:27,100
come on chicken.

2404
01:29:27,100 --> 01:29:28,333
(clucking)

2405
01:29:28,333 --> 01:29:30,167
- [Joel] I wonder
what he's thinking.

2406
01:29:31,533 --> 01:29:32,867
- [Crow] Ditch her, go run!

2407
01:29:35,100 --> 01:29:36,767
- [Tom] You are going to die.

2408
01:29:38,367 --> 01:29:42,200
I am going to kill you.
- Ken!

2409
01:29:42,200 --> 01:29:43,033
Ken!

2410
01:29:44,300 --> 01:29:45,400
- [Tom] Rita!

2411
01:29:47,267 --> 01:29:49,267
(soldier screaming)
(gasps)

2412
01:29:49,267 --> 01:29:51,333
He killed the tree.

2413
01:29:51,333 --> 01:29:52,867
(weapons firing)

2414
01:29:52,867 --> 01:29:55,267
(Ken groans)

2415
01:29:58,500 --> 01:29:59,333
- Rita!

2416
01:29:59,333 --> 01:30:00,700
- [All] Meter maid!

2417
01:30:00,700 --> 01:30:02,133
- Rita, are you all right?

2418
01:30:03,533 --> 01:30:05,767
- [Crow] I killed your
other brothers by the way.

2419
01:30:05,767 --> 01:30:06,600
- Ken.

2420
01:30:07,633 --> 01:30:08,467
Traitor.

2421
01:30:09,767 --> 01:30:11,833
It was you who fired that shot.

2422
01:30:11,833 --> 01:30:13,167
It was you.

2423
01:30:14,933 --> 01:30:17,067
- [Joel] Wait, let
me explain, oh, darn.

2424
01:30:17,067 --> 01:30:18,167
- [Ken] Rita!

2425
01:30:20,167 --> 01:30:24,400
The most important part
of me just died too.

2426
01:30:24,400 --> 01:30:25,500
- [Crow] Well, at
least he gets to keep

2427
01:30:25,500 --> 01:30:27,167
that swell Star Trek stuff.

2428
01:30:28,567 --> 01:30:31,567
- [Tom] Well honey, looks like
I'm gonna have to gut you.

2429
01:30:31,567 --> 01:30:33,500
- [Joel and Crow] Oh!

2430
01:30:33,500 --> 01:30:35,667
- [Joel] That's it, make
it look like a robbery.

2431
01:30:35,667 --> 01:30:36,500
- I heard gunfire.

2432
01:30:36,500 --> 01:30:37,733
Are you all right?

2433
01:30:37,733 --> 01:30:39,000
- [Crow] Where have you been?

2434
01:30:39,000 --> 01:30:40,000
- [Ken] I'm fine,
the others are dead.

2435
01:30:41,567 --> 01:30:43,233
- Who's she, what
happened to her?

2436
01:30:43,233 --> 01:30:45,867
- A Kararun girl got
caught in the crossfire.

2437
01:30:45,867 --> 01:30:47,133
- [Crow] Huh, bummer.

2438
01:30:47,133 --> 01:30:48,333
- It's late, we
better get going.

2439
01:30:48,333 --> 01:30:49,967
There's nothing we can do here.

2440
01:30:49,967 --> 01:30:50,967
- [Tom] But I'm thirsty again.

2441
01:30:50,967 --> 01:30:52,333
- [Crow] Will you get going?

2442
01:30:53,800 --> 01:30:55,433
- [Ken] Good-bye,
Rita, good-bye.

2443
01:30:57,733 --> 01:30:58,733
- [Joel] Come
back, I'm not dead.

2444
01:30:58,733 --> 01:31:01,367
You didn't check for a pulse.

2445
01:31:03,033 --> 01:31:05,533
(tense music)

2446
01:31:09,700 --> 01:31:11,567
- [Crow] Next time
on Twin Peaks.

2447
01:31:14,133 --> 01:31:16,033
- Help, Ken.
- I've got you.

2448
01:31:19,333 --> 01:31:21,200
- [Tom] Come 'ere you, come on.

2449
01:31:22,100 --> 01:31:25,167
- [Joel] Let him go, drop him.

2450
01:31:25,167 --> 01:31:27,600
- [Tom] Would you take those
rocks out of your pockets?

2451
01:31:27,600 --> 01:31:28,600
- [Crow] Rock climbing, Joel.

2452
01:31:28,600 --> 01:31:29,700
- [Tom] Rock climbing.

2453
01:31:35,600 --> 01:31:37,200
- [Crow] Caesar Romero?

2454
01:31:37,200 --> 01:31:38,267
Edmund Hillary?

2455
01:31:39,200 --> 01:31:40,400
(dramatic music)

2456
01:31:40,400 --> 01:31:42,567
- [Joel] Oh, they're
down there, jump for it!

2457
01:31:44,500 --> 01:31:46,667
- Hey, hey, hey!

2458
